terest definition for RWTH Aachen — 5th nationally at 45 113 students (DESTATIS GENESIS, WS 2024/25). The second twin built on the Nordrhein-Westfalen adapter, and the one that made writing it worthwhile: NRW holds Köln (3), Aachen (5), Münster (7), Bochum (11), Duisburg-Essen (12) and Bonn (14), so one survey authority reaches more of the national top twenty than any other.",HM="aachen",GM={name:{de:"RWTH Aachen",en:"RWTH Aachen University"},region:{de:"Aachen, Nordrhein-Westfalen",en:"Aachen, North Rhine-Westphalia"},timezone:"Europe/Berlin"},VM=[],jM="Empty, deliberately — the state OTH shipped in and the one FAU and Köln are in. A lens may only be declared where its data requirements can be met (`world.test.ts` enforces it). RWTH publishes no timetable this project can read and no indoor geometry has been probed, so occupancy, staffing and quality are impossible; `condition` would mean seeding an invented Sanierungsstau for a named real university.",WM={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:6.0442,east:6.0853,south:50.7718,north:50.7937,$comment:"HIGH-RESOLUTION CORE, ~2.89 x 2.44 km. From the campus cluster find_campus_areas.py resolved out of OpenStreetMap (config/campus-candidates.json, HS148: 39 areas, discriminating tokens rwth/rheinisch/westfalische) plus ~250 m of margin. It holds BOTH halves of RWTH, which is the point: the historic Templergraben core in the east (Audimax, Zentralbibliothek, Sammelbau Maschinenwesen, Reiff-Museum) and the Melaten/Campus-West research estate in the west (Physik, Chemie, E.ON Energy Research Center), about 2.5 km apart with Aachen West station between them."},$M={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:5.93,east:6.2,south:50.698,north:50.868,$comment:"COARSE TERRAIN SHELL, ~19.0 x 18.9 km. Aachen sits in a bowl and the shell is doing real work here — the Eifel foothills close the horizon to the south and the Lousberg stands over the city to the north.\n\n⚠️ THIS SHELL CROSSES TWO NATIONAL BORDERS. Its western edge reaches into Belgium and the Netherlands, where Geobasis NRW publishes nothing at all. `fetch_nrw.py` reports those tiles as 'not published' and carries on, which is correct — a tile outside the state is a fact about NRW, not a failure — and the Copernicus shell covers the gap. The CORE (6.044-6.085 E) is entirely inside Germany, so the high-resolution twin itself has no hole in it."},qM="EPSG:25832",XM="DHHN2016",YM={min:145,max:275,$measured:!0,$comment:`MEASURED 2026-08-10 by build_terrain.py over the core: 151.69 .. 264.04 m, from 16 Geobasis NRW DGM1 tiles at 100% coverage (grid 1498 x 1276 at 2 m). Left slightly loose around the measurement so a re-run after an NRW update does not trip the plausibility gate over a decimetre.

112 m of relief — by far the most of the four twins added for the top-ten set (FAU 36 m, Köln 25 m, Münster 22 m) and the only one where the hypsometric ramp and the terrain shading genuinely do work. Aachen sits in a bowl and the campus climbs its side, which is also why the two halves of RWTH are at visibly different heights.

The starting guess was 150-300: the floor was very nearly right and the ceiling 36 m too generous, which is the same failure as FAU's 250-450 in a milder form — reasoning about a city's surroundings rather than about the box actually being rendered.`},KM={maxPx:4096,$comment:"Long side of the DOP mosaic, via the Geobasis NRW WMS (layer nw_dop_rgb, 10 cm source). NOT larger: at 8192 px the mipmap chain is ~300 MB, which Chromium accepts and then silently samples BLACK."},ZM={sourceResolutionM:1,renderResolutionM:2,renderDecimation:2,$comment:"Geobasis NRW DGM1, resampled to a 2 m heightmap, mesh decimated 2x -> 4 m posting. NRW publishes DGM1 already as a float32 GeoTIFF carrying the ModelTiepoint/ModelPixelScale pair build_terrain.py reads, so nothing is converted between download and grid."},QM={sourceResolutionM:30,renderResolutionM:30,renderDecimation:3,transitionBandM:250,$comment:"Copernicus GLO-30 -> ~90 m posting. transitionBandM is written in metres for readability but MUST be applied as a fraction of the core (CORE_FADE_FRACTION ~0.08), never absolute."},JM={probedOn:"2026-08-10",roomsFound:0,$comment:"⚠️ Named `indoorProbe` and NOT `rooms` — a `rooms` block in this engine MEANS real indoor geometry exists and drives the hero-building explode. Nothing has been probed for RWTH, so buildings stay solid and the app says so rather than inventing interiors."},eE=[{id:"audimax",name:"Audimax",lat:50.78004,lon:6.0762},{id:"zentralbibliothek",name:"Zentralbibliothek",lat:50.77899,lon:6.08005},{id:"templergraben",name:"Sammelbau Templergraben",lat:50.77744,lon:6.07929},{id:"maschinenwesen",name:"Sammelbau Maschinenwesen",lat:50.77763,lon:6.08061},{id:"rogowski",name:"Rogowski-Institut",lat:50.77807,lon:6.07648},{id:"mensa",name:"Mensa Academica",lat:50.78169,lon:6.0764},{id:"reiff",name:"Reiff-Museum",lat:50.77731,lon:6.07684},{id:"couvenhalle",name:"Couvenhalle",lat:50.77658,lon:6.07798},{id:"aerodynamik",name:"Institut für Aerodynamik",lat:50.77866,lon:6.07659},{id:"it_center",name:"IT Center",lat:50.78093,lon:6.06513},{id:"physik",name:"Hörsaal Physik",lat:50.78133,lon:6.04842},{id:"eon_erc",name:"E.ON Energy Research Center",lat:50.78931,lon:6.05165},{id:"bahnhof",name:"Aachen West",lat:50.78072,lon:6.06961,kind:"station"}],tE="Resolved 2026-08-10 from OpenStreetMap via Overpass BY TAG AND OPERATOR — `amenity=university`, `building=university`, buildings whose operator matches RWTH, libraries and stations inside the core box — and not by remembered name, for the reason Tübingen's config records at length. 120 named elements came back; the thirteen above are the ones that carry the campus's shape, deliberately split across both halves so the tour does not imply RWTH is only its historic core.",nE={authority:"Geobasis NRW (Bezirksregierung Köln)",licence:"Datenlizenz Deutschland – Zero – Version 2.0",licenceUrl:"https://www.govdata.de/dl-de/zero-2-0",attribution:"Datenquelle: Land NRW (Geobasis NRW), dl-de/zero-2-0",downloadBase:"https://www.opengeodata.nrw.de/produkte/geobasis/",dopWms:"https://www.wms.nrw.de/geobasis/wms_nw_dop",$comment:"pipeline.py's `in_nordrhein_westfalen` predicate keys on the string 'Geobasis NRW' here, so this field is load-bearing rather than decoration. dl-de/ZERO-2-0 requires no attribution at all; it is given anyway, because every other source in this app is credited and a licence that permits silence is not a reason to be silent about where a campus came from."},iE={authority:"ESA / DLR / Airbus Defence and Space — Copernicus DEM GLO-30",licence:"Copernicus DEM free licence (worldwide, free reuse with the prescribed notice)",licenceUrl:"https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM",attribution:"produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved",$attributionComment:"The ADAPTED-DATA form of the notice, which is prescribed rather than stylistic: the pipeline resamples the tile onto a UTM grid and shifts it onto the core's vertical datum.",cogUrlTemplate:"https://copernicus-dem-30m.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM.tif",tiles:["N50_E005","N50_E006"],$tilesComment:"TWO tiles. The shell runs 5.93-6.20 E, so it crosses the 6 E meridian even though Aachen itself sits comfortably inside E006; latitude needs only N50. A missing tile does not raise an error — it renders as a flat shelf across that side of the horizon, which here would be the Belgian border."},aE=[{placeId:"audimax",captionKey:"tour.aachen.audimax",rangeM:700,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"templergraben",captionKey:"tour.aachen.templergraben",rangeM:600,holdMs:6e3},{placeId:"it_center",captionKey:"tour.aachen.westcampus",rangeM:1100,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"eon_erc",captionKey:"tour.aachen.melaten",rangeM:800,holdMs:6e3}],sE={$comment:FM,id:HM,site:GM,lenses:VM,$lensesComment:jM,bbox:WM,shell:$M,workingCrs:qM,verticalDatum:XM,elevationRangeM:YM,drape:KM,grids:ZM,shellGrids:QM,indoorProbe:JM,focusPlaces:eE,$focusPlacesComment:tE,geobasis:nE,shellGeobasis:iE,tour:aE},rE="Area of interest definition for FAU Erlangen-Nürnberg — the fifth twin, and the first built for the 'top ten German universities by student numbers' set (PLAN §37). FAU is 9th on that list at 40 382 students (DESTATIS GENESIS, WS 2024/25, via config/universities.json) and was chosen FIRST for a reason that is about cost rather than importance: it is in Bayern, so the LDBV pipeline that already serves OTH, LMU and Garching applies unchanged and no new survey authority has to be reverse-engineered. Köln, Aachen and Münster are larger and needed a Nordrhein-Westfalen adapter before they could be attempted at all.",oE="fau-erlangen",lE={name:{de:"FAU Erlangen-Nürnberg",en:"FAU Erlangen-Nürnberg"},region:{de:"Erlangen, Bayern",en:"Erlangen, Bavaria"},timezone:"Europe/Berlin"},cE="⚠️ THE UNIVERSITY IS ERLANGEN-*NÜRNBERG* AND THIS AOI IS ERLANGEN ONLY. FAU teaches in both cities, ~17 km apart, plus Fürth. Covering both in one AOI would mean a ~20 x 12 km core — an order of magnitude more terrain, buildings and drape than any AOI here, for a corridor that is mostly other people's city. So this twin is honest about its extent in its own id (`fau-erlangen`) rather than claiming the whole institution, exactly as `garching` does not claim to be all of TUM. The Nürnberg sites (WiSo, Erziehungswissenschaften) are NOT in this box and no part of the app should imply otherwise.",uE=[],dE="Empty, deliberately, and the same state OTH shipped in first. A lens may only be declared where its data requirements can be met (`world.test.ts` enforces this and failed the original engine fork for exactly this reason). FAU publishes no timetable, so `occupancy`, `staffing` and `quality` are impossible; the indoor probe below found nothing, so room analytics are impossible; and `condition` would mean seeding an invented Sanierungsstau for a named real university, which is a decision to take deliberately rather than by copying Tübingen's block. Lenses return when data lands.",hE={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:11.001,east:11.0348,south:49.5673,north:49.6036,$comment:"HIGH-RESOLUTION CORE, ~2.44 x 4.04 km. Derived from the two campus clusters that find_campus_areas.py resolved out of OpenStreetMap (config/campus-candidates.json, HS131: 33 areas around Freyeslebenstraße and 25 around Röthelheim/Innenstadt), unioned and given ~250 m of margin. Tall rather than wide because that is the shape FAU actually has in Erlangen: the Technische Fakultät sits on the Südgelände at 49.570-49.582, the Schloss and Kollegienhaus are in the Innenstadt at 49.597-49.601, and Röthelheim lies between them. Comparable in area to OTH (3.07 x 2.84 km) and LMU (3.12 x 3.83 km)."},fE={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:10.91,east:11.13,south:49.5,north:49.67,$comment:"COARSE TERRAIN SHELL, ~15.9 x 18.9 km. Reaches the Rathsberg and the Burgberg ridge north-east of the city, the Regnitz and the Main-Donau-Kanal to the west, and the Sebalder Reichswald to the south — which is what actually closes the horizon from the Südgelände. Stops well short of Nürnberg: the shell exists to give the core a believable surround, not to render a second city at 90 m posting."},mE="EPSG:25832",pE="DHHN2016",gE={min:260,max:315,$measured:!0,$comment:`MEASURED 2026-08-07 by build_terrain.py over the core: 268.34 .. 304.73 m, from 20 LDBV DGM1 tiles at 100% coverage (grid 1276 x 2051 at 2 m). The bracket is left slightly loose around the measurement so a re-run after an LDBV update does not trip the plausibility gate over a decimetre; uint16 quantisation over 55 m is ~0.8 mm.

⚠️ THE FIRST VALUE HERE WAS A GUESS OF 250-450 AND IT WAS BADLY WRONG. Reasoning from published figures — the Regnitz at roughly 280 m, the Rathsberg ridge in the 380s — produced a bracket almost four times the real spread, because the RIDGE IS IN THE SHELL AND NOT IN THE CORE. Erlangen's core is genuinely flat: 36 m of relief over 4 km. Shipping the guess would have spent two thirds of the hypsometric ramp on elevations this AOI does not contain, which is the exact failure Tübingen's config records. The shell does reach 526 m; that is a different grid and a different range.

Ground heights at the resolved focus places came out at Erlangen Hbf 278.2 m, Chemikum 285.8 m, Physikum 287.6 m, Felix-Klein-Gebäude 292.2 m — all plausible, which is a second confirmation that the focus coordinates landed on the campus rather than somewhere the name also matched.`},vE={maxPx:4096,$comment:"Long side of the DOP20 mosaic, via the LDBV WMS. NOT larger: at 8192 px the mipmap chain is ~300 MB, which Chromium accepts and then silently samples BLACK. The drape texture must be loaded with flipY=false and WITHOUT mipmaps (PLAN §5.5)."},bE={sourceResolutionM:1,renderResolutionM:2,renderDecimation:2,$comment:"LDBV DGM1 source, resampled to a 2 m heightmap, mesh decimated 2x -> 4 m posting. The same tier as every other AOI in this repo, so the renderer keeps one code path and the twins stay visually comparable."},yE={sourceResolutionM:30,renderResolutionM:30,renderDecimation:3,transitionBandM:250,$comment:"Copernicus GLO-30 -> ~90 m posting. transitionBandM is written in metres for readability but MUST be applied as a fraction of the core (CORE_FADE_FRACTION ~0.08), never absolute — an absolute band tuned for a 9 km alpine AOI once ate 43% of a 2 km campus."},xE={probedOn:"2026-08-07",roomsFound:0,$comment:"⚠️ Named `indoorProbe` and NOT `rooms`, because in this engine a `rooms` block MEANS 'real indoor geometry exists' and drives the hero-building explode. FAU has no NavigaTUM equivalent and no published per-floor plans that this project has found, so buildings here stay solid and the app says so rather than inventing interiors — the same answer OTH gave before its floor plans were OCR'd."},_E=[{id:"schloss",name:"Schloss Erlangen",lat:49.59788,lon:11.00452},{id:"kollegienhaus",name:"Kollegienhaus",lat:49.59731,lon:11.00708},{id:"schlossgarten",name:"Schlossgarten",lat:49.59822,lon:11.00737},{id:"hoersaal_c",name:"Hörsaal C",lat:49.60092,lon:11.01654},{id:"technische_fakultaet",name:"Technische Fakultät",lat:49.57335,lon:11.02598},{id:"informatik",name:"Informatik und Rechenzentrum (RRZE)",lat:49.57375,lon:11.02738},{id:"mensa_sued",name:"Mensa und Bibliothek Südgelände",lat:49.57455,lon:11.02951},{id:"chemikum",name:"Chemikum",lat:49.57812,lon:11.02858},{id:"physikum",name:"Physikum",lat:49.58029,lon:11.02933},{id:"biologikum",name:"Biologikum",lat:49.57937,lon:11.0292},{id:"felix_klein",name:"Felix-Klein-Gebäude",lat:49.57385,lon:11.03023},{id:"roethelheim",name:"Röthelheim-Campus",lat:49.59518,lon:11.0236},{id:"bahnhof",name:"Erlangen Hbf",lat:49.59607,lon:11.00159,kind:"station"}],SE="Resolved 2026-08-07 from OpenStreetMap via Overpass BY TAG AND OPERATOR — not from memory, and not by name. Tübingen's config records why: a name match there returned a student fraternity for the castle and a bookshop for the Hölderlinturm. The query asked for `amenity=university`, `building=university`, university-operated buildings, stations and named parks inside the core box, and every coordinate above is the centre of a returned element (Schloss Erlangen way/27883772 and Kollegienhaus way/27883773 both carry `operator=FAU Friedrich-Alexander-Universität`; Erlangen Hbf is node/4530820005).\n\n⚠️ ONE TRAP WORTH RECORDING. The obvious anchor — `relation/3569139`, literally named 'Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg' — has its centre at 49.51864, 11.05961, which is open country roughly 7 km SOUTH of this AOI. It is correct: the relation spans Erlangen AND Nürnberg, so its centroid falls in the gap between the two cities. Anchoring the AOI on the feature that carries the university's own name would have put the entire twin in a field. The centroid of a multi-site relation is not a campus.",wE={authority:"Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung (LDBV)",licence:"CC BY 4.0",licenceUrl:"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/deed.de",attribution:"Datenquelle: Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung – www.geodaten.bayern.de [Daten bearbeitet]",downloadBase:"https://download1.bayernwolke.de",downloadMirror:"https://download2.bayernwolke.de",metalinkBase:"https://geodaten.bayern.de/odd",$comment:"Identical to the OTH, LMU and Garching AOIs — Erlangen is in Bayern, so the same survey authority, portal and licence apply, and pipeline.py's `in_bavaria` predicate keys on this string to select the LDBV steps. This is the entire reason FAU was built before the larger NRW universities: no new fetcher. The attribution is not optional."},ME={authority:"ESA / DLR / Airbus Defence and Space — Copernicus DEM GLO-30",licence:"Copernicus DEM free licence (worldwide, free reuse with the prescribed notice)",licenceUrl:"https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM",attribution:"produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved",$attributionComment:"The ADAPTED-DATA form of the notice, which is prescribed rather than stylistic: the pipeline resamples the tile onto a UTM grid and shifts it onto the core's vertical datum, so it is unambiguously modified.",cogUrlTemplate:"https://copernicus-dem-30m.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM.tif",tiles:["N49_E010","N49_E011"],$tilesComment:"TWO tiles. The shell runs 10.91-11.13 E, so it crosses the 11 E meridian and the western strip falls in E010 even though Erlangen itself is comfortably inside E011. Latitude needs only N49 (49.50-49.67). A missing tile does not raise an error — it renders as a flat shelf across that side of the horizon, which is why the crossing is worked out here rather than discovered on screen."},EE=[{placeId:"schloss",captionKey:"tour.fau.schloss",rangeM:700,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"technische_fakultaet",captionKey:"tour.fau.technische",rangeM:1100,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"informatik",captionKey:"tour.fau.informatik",rangeM:500,holdMs:6e3},{placeId:"roethelheim",captionKey:"tour.fau.roethelheim",rangeM:800,holdMs:6e3}],TE={$comment:rE,id:oE,site:lE,$nameComment:cE,lenses:uE,$lensesComment:dE,bbox:hE,shell:fE,workingCrs:mE,verticalDatum:pE,elevationRangeM:gE,drape:vE,grids:bE,shellGrids:yE,indoorProbe:xE,focusPlaces:_E,$focusPlacesComment:SE,geobasis:wE,shellGeobasis:ME,tour:EE},AE="Area of interest definition. The location is configuration — nothing about a place is hard-coded in the app, which is why eight universities ship from one build. This one arrived with the engine fork and was its first instance. ⚠️ Its interiors are governed by config/release.json: `navigatumData` decides whether the rooms carry TUM's own semantics, an invented week, or nothing at all.",RE="garching",CE={name:{de:"TUM Garching Forschungszentrum",en:"TUM Garching Research Campus"},region:{de:"Garching bei München, Bayern",en:"Garching near Munich, Bavaria"},timezone:"Europe/Berlin"},NE=["occupancy","flow"],DE="tum",LE="⚠️ THIS ONE LINE TURNS THE PLANNER ON — `hasPlanner` is `Boolean(schedulerSite)` — so it must never be added without a matching entry in `SITE_BASES` in src/api/scheduler.ts. `apiBase()` falls back to the single-backend URL for an unknown site, which is another university's container: Garching would render TUM's campus over OTH's timetable, confidently and without an error. `sites.test.ts` asserts the pair. Garching is also the only site here whose timetable is REAL — 1,470 published TUMonline bookings, reshaped by tools/data/build_tum_dataset.py — while its lecturers and cohorts are invented, because TUMonline publishes neither. The app refuses lecturer questions on this site for exactly that reason; see `teacher_attribution_invented`.",UE="PLAN D6: lenses are AOI-scoped. Garching carries `occupancy` because it is the only campus in this project with real indoor data (see `rooms` below). It does NOT carry `condition` — a Sanierungsstau story on a research campus whose buildings are actively funded would be the least credible version of that conversation, and Tübingen's historic stock is the honest place for it.",OE={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:11.657,east:11.69,south:48.258,north:48.276,$comment:"HIGH-RESOLUTION CORE, ~2.44 x 2.00 km. Photoreal tier: DGM1 + DOP20 drape + LoD2 + trees. Deliberately tight: this is a campus, not a massif, and the camera spends its life between 200 m and 1500 m above a 2 km square. The box is the one the indoor-data probe used (2026-07-30), widened by ~250 m on each side so the Boltzmannstraße frontage, the U-Bahn portal and the Mensa forecourt all have margin rather than sitting on the edge. Every resolved focus place below lies inside it: lon 11.6678-11.6759, lat 48.2624-48.2688."},IE={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:11.55,east:11.79,south:48.19,north:48.33,$comment:"COARSE TERRAIN SHELL, ~17.8 x 15.6 km. Terrain only, fading into aerial haze. Garching is on the Münchner Schotterebene and the relief is almost nil, so the shell is doing a different job here than in an Alpine AOI: it is not there for drama, it is there so the photoreal 2 km square does not end in a cliff of nothing. It reaches the Isar to the east, Garching town and Hochbrück to the south, and the edge of Munich — which is what a viewer looking north from the campus actually sees."},PE="EPSG:25832",kE="DHHN2016",zE={min:460,max:510,$comment:"MEASURED 2026-07-30 by build_terrain.py: 464.9 .. 484.7 m, i.e. ~20 m of relief across the entire core, versus 1400 m in the Alpine AOI this engine was built for. (An earlier draft of this note guessed 478-490 m; the model disagreed, and the model wins.) The bracket is left deliberately loose around the measurement so a re-run after an LDBV data update does not trip the plausibility gate over a decimetre. CONSEQUENCE, and it drives Phase 1: every hillshade constant tuned for a mountain does nothing here. On flat ground the realism has to come from the DOP20 drape, the LoD2 roofs and CAST SHADOWS, not from terrain shading. The uint16 quantisation over a 50 m bracket is ~0.8 mm, far finer than the source, so nothing is lost by keeping it loose."},BE={$comment:"PLAN rule 1 — the registration gate. The Alpine strategy (>=5 published summits inside the core) is IMPOSSIBLE here: an Overpass probe of this bbox on 2026-07-30 returned zero `ele`-tagged nodes of any kind, and with 20 m of relief a two-kilometre horizontal error would still sample ~475 m. Rather than delete the gate, verify_registration.py proves registration from the evidence that does exist — see its module docstring for checks A-F.",minCoveragePct:99.5,toleranceM:3,shellToleranceM:12,$shellToleranceComment:"Looser because the shell is Copernicus GLO-30, a SURFACE model: it includes canopy and buildings, so a control point in a built-up or wooded 30 m cell reads high by design. This is not a softer test, it is the correct test for that product.",maxSeamOffsetM:3,$maxSeamOffsetComment:"The strongest check available on flat ground. build_shell.py measures the offset between the LDBV airborne-laser BARE-EARTH model and the Copernicus satellite SURFACE model in the overlap ring, on open ground only. Measured 2026-07-30: +0.17 m. Two independent surveys with different sensors, different vertical datums and different acquisition decades agreeing to 17 cm is not something a misplaced grid produces.",minPeaks:5,controlPoints:[{name:"Garching bei München (Ortsmittelpunkt)",lat:48.2513878,lon:11.6509662,publishedM:482,source:"OSM node/240084687 place=town ele=482"},{name:"Höhenpunkt Dietersheim",lat:48.2943186,lon:11.6535492,publishedM:468.04,source:"OSM node/267951933 ele=468.04"},{name:"Messstation Garching 2",lat:48.2511325,lon:11.6405778,publishedM:481.79,source:"OSM node/11570554013 man_made=monitoring_station ele=481.79"}],$controlPointsComment:"Resolved 2026-07-30 by an Overpass query for any `ele`-tagged element in and around the core. All three lie in the SHELL rather than the core, because the core has none — that is fine, they still prove the model describes this place and not another. The two carrying two decimal places are surveyed values rather than rounded map labels, which is why they are worth more than the town node. TWO CANDIDATES WERE REJECTED and are recorded here so they are not silently re-added: `PSW automotive engineering GmbH` (node/2245285380, ele=510) is ~30 m above surrounding ground and is almost certainly a building height mis-tagged as an elevation; `amenity=recycling` (node/9180239919) carries ele=0, which is not an elevation at all. A control point is only a control point if somebody surveyed it."},FE={maxPx:4096,$comment:"Long side of the DOP20 mosaic, in pixels. For this 2.52 km core that is ~0.62 m per pixel — still far finer than the 4 m terrain mesh beneath it, and sharp enough to read road markings and parking bays. NOT larger, and the reason is rendering rather than photography: the drape is uploaded with mipmaps, and at 8192 px the chain is ~300 MB. Chromium accepted the texture, silently failed to finish the chain, and sampled BLACK — the entire campus rendered as a black lozenge under correctly-lit buildings, with nothing logged anywhere. See tools/geodata/fetch_dop20.py."},HE={sourceResolutionM:1,renderResolutionM:2,renderDecimation:2,$comment:"1 m DGM1 source, resampled to a 2 m heightmap, mesh decimated 2x -> 4 m posting. FINER than the Alpine AOI (4 m / 16 m) and deliberately so: the subject is 2 km across rather than 9 km, the camera gets much closer to the ground, and kerbs, steps and the Mensa terrace are the scale that reads. Roughly 1220 x 1000 heightmap samples (~2.4 MB) and ~305k mesh vertices — cheaper than the Alpine core despite the finer grid, because the area is 16x smaller."},GE={sourceResolutionM:30,renderResolutionM:30,renderDecimation:3,transitionBandM:900,$comment:"Copernicus DEM GLO-30 -> ~90 m posting. transitionBandM is narrower than the Alpine AOI's 1200 m because the core is only 2 km wide and a 1200 m band would consume more than half of it. The two tiers do NOT share a vertical datum (core = DHHN2016 bare earth, shell = EGM2008 surface model including canopy and buildings), so the shell is shifted by an offset MEASURED in the overlap ring, never assumed to be zero. On ground this flat the seam is far more forgiving than in the Alps — but the colour seam is not, so the land-cover fade still matters."},VE=[{id:"garching",name:"Campus Garching",lat:48.26538,lon:11.67152},{id:"mw",name:"Maschinenwesen",lat:48.26562,lon:11.66921},{id:"mi",name:"Mathematik / Informatik",lat:48.26252,lon:11.66808},{id:"physik",name:"Physik",lat:48.26725,lon:11.6759},{id:"chemie",name:"Chemie",lat:48.2688,lon:11.66979},{id:"frm2",name:"FRM II",lat:48.26574,lon:11.67569},{id:"galileo",name:"Galileo / Conference Center",lat:48.26539,lon:11.67211},{id:"ubahn",name:"U-Bahn Garching-Forschungszentrum",lat:48.2647408,lon:11.6714052,kind:"station"}],jE="Resolved 2026-07-30 from the NavigaTUM API (/api/locations/{id}) and, for the U-Bahn station, from OpenStreetMap node/2643681873 — NOT recalled. Same rule as the Alpine AOI: a coordinate is only verified once something independent agrees with it, which for this AOI is step `verify` sampling the built terrain at each place. NavigaTUM reports its own coords.source per entry: `navigatum` for the curated campus/faculty anchors above, `roomfinder` for the individual building parts in `rooms.exploreBuildings`.",WE={$comment:"PLAN §2.1 and Phase 2. This block is what makes `occupancy` possible at all, and it is the only AOI in the project that can carry it. THREE independent open sources join cleanly on the TUM room code: OSM indoor room POLYGONS carry `ref:tum` (e.g. 5606.EG.041), NavigaTUM supplies the room SEMANTICS for that code, and the NavigaTUM calendar supplies REAL TUMonline bookings. Verified live 2026-07-30 — see PLAN §2.1 for the counts.",codePattern:"^\\d{4}\\.[A-Z0-9]{2}\\.\\d{3}$",osmRefKey:"ref:tum",navigatumBase:"https://nav.tum.de/api",navigatumCampusId:"garching",referenceSemester:{id:"ws2025",startDate:"2025-10-13",endDate:"2026-02-07",$comment:"The window baked into the Lakehouse (PLAN D4). A FULL semester rather than a sample week, so 'Auslastung' is a semester statistic and not an anecdote about one Tuesday. Lecture-free weeks are included and are visible in the result — that is the point, not a defect."},exploreBuildings:[{code:"5501",name:"MW – Mechatronik",osmRooms:382,navigatumRooms:462,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5502",name:"MW – Werkstoffe und Verarbeitung",osmRooms:260,navigatumRooms:435,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5503",name:"MW – Produktionstechnik",osmRooms:347,navigatumRooms:419,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5504",name:"MW – Verfahrenstechnik",osmRooms:382,navigatumRooms:466,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5505",name:"MW – Maschinentechnik",osmRooms:331,navigatumRooms:419,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5506",name:"MW – Luft- und Raumfahrt",osmRooms:395,navigatumRooms:480,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5507",name:"MW – Energietechnik",osmRooms:275,navigatumRooms:346,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3","4"]},{code:"5508",name:"MW – Hörsaal West",osmRooms:30,navigatumRooms:39,levels:["-1","0","1","2"]},{code:"5510",name:"Hörsaal, Bibliothek u. Verwaltung",osmRooms:241,navigatumRooms:291,levels:["-2","-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5514",name:"MW – Nebengebäude",osmRooms:15,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["0","1"]},{code:"5515",name:"MW – Nebengebäude",osmRooms:18,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["0","1"]},{code:"5532",name:"StudiTUM Garching",osmRooms:41,navigatumRooms:83,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3","4"]},{code:"5602",name:"MI – Hörsaal 1",osmRooms:2,navigatumRooms:4,levels:["0"]},{code:"5604",name:"MI – Finger 04",osmRooms:125,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5606",name:"MI – Finger 06",osmRooms:161,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5607",name:"MI – Finger 07",osmRooms:163,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5608",name:"MI – Finger 08",osmRooms:10,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["0"]},{code:"5609",name:"MI – Finger 09",osmRooms:162,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5610",name:"MI – Finger 10",osmRooms:145,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5611",name:"MI – Finger 11",osmRooms:143,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5612",name:"MI – Finger 12",osmRooms:146,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"5613",name:"MI – Finger 13",osmRooms:149,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["-1","0","1","2","3"]},{code:"8120",name:"Galileo",osmRooms:7,navigatumRooms:null,levels:["0","1","2","3"]}],$exploreBuildingsComment:"MEASURED counts, corrected 2026-07-30 from a complete `out geom` fetch of every `indoor=room` in the core, deduplicated by OSM id. They replace an earlier set taken from a quadrant-split probe that both over-counted some buildings (5506 read 429, actually 395) and MISSED THE ENTIRE MI COMPLEX (5602-5613, ~1 200 rooms) because those quadrants returned nothing. Recorded here so Phase 2 has a regression baseline: if the pipeline yields materially fewer rooms than `osmRooms`, the join or the fetch has silently broken. `osmRooms` < `navigatumRooms` is EXPECTED and not an error — OSM indoor mapping is volunteer work and runs at roughly 80-90% of the official room list. `navigatumRooms` is null where the official per-building count was not published separately (the MI and MW 'fingers' are reported by NavigaTUM as one joined building). Buildings absent from this list are absent from OSM indoor mapping entirely; they stay SOLID in the app and say so. No room is ever invented to fill a gap (PLAN §0).",heroBuilding:"5506",$heroBuildingComment:"The scripted demo path. 5506 has the highest OSM room count (395) in the MW complex, whose eight wings are physically connected — so the camera can explode one wing while the rest of the complex stays solid as context. The MI complex (5604-5613) is a strong second: fewer rooms per finger, but it is the building with the slide and is the more recognisable of the two.",storeyHeightM:3.6,$storeyHeightComment:"Fallback only. Phase 2 derives per-building storey height from the LoD2 total height divided by the OSM level count; this value is used where that fails. It is the weakest number in the pipeline and it is the one that shows — get it wrong and exploded floors interpenetrate. Override per building here when Phase 2 finds a bad fit.",seatDensityM2:{Hörsaal:.8,Seminarraum:2,Übungsraum:2,Unterrichtsraum:2,Studentenarbeitsraum:3,"Praktikumsraum - EDV":3,Büro:12},$seatDensityComment:"⚠️ SYNTHETIC. Seat counts are NOT published: the `capacity` tag is present on ~1.5% of OSM rooms and NavigaTUM does not expose one. Seats are therefore DERIVED as floor area / density, and every figure computed from them is marked synthetic in the UI (PLAN §6). The densities are ordinary German planning rules of thumb, not a survey of these rooms. Room AREA itself is honest — it is computed by shoelace from the real OSM polygon in EPSG:25832."},$E={authority:"Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung (LDBV)",licence:"CC BY 4.0",licenceUrl:"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/deed.de",attribution:"Datenquelle: Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung – www.geodaten.bayern.de [Daten bearbeitet]",downloadBase:"https://download1.bayernwolke.de",downloadMirror:"https://download2.bayernwolke.de",metalinkBase:"https://geodaten.bayern.de/odd"},qE={authority:"ESA / DLR / Airbus Defence and Space — Copernicus DEM GLO-30",licence:"Copernicus DEM free licence (worldwide, free reuse with the prescribed notice)",licenceUrl:"https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM",attribution:"produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved",$attributionComment:"The ADAPTED-DATA form of the notice, which is prescribed rather than stylistic: the pipeline resamples the tile onto a UTM grid and shifts it onto the core's vertical datum, so it is unambiguously modified and the plain © form would be the wrong notice.",cogUrlTemplate:"https://copernicus-dem-30m.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM.tif",tiles:["N48_E011"],$tilesComment:"The single N48/E011 tile covers the entire shell (48-49 N, 11-12 E). Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFF, so the fetcher range-requests the AOI window rather than pulling the whole file."},XE={osm:{authority:"OpenStreetMap contributors",licence:"ODbL 1.0",licenceUrl:"https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/",attribution:"© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0"},navigatum:{authority:"NavigaTUM (TUM-Dev) / TUMonline",projectUrl:"https://github.com/TUM-Dev/NavigaTUM",projectLicence:"GPL-3.0 (software)",$comment:"⚠️ OPEN ITEM, PLAN §7. The GPL-3.0 licence covers the NavigaTUM SOFTWARE; the room and calendar DATA originate from TUMonline and their redistribution terms are NOT yet established. Internal demonstration is fine. This MUST be resolved before any public gallery release, and before the baked semester snapshot is committed anywhere public."}},YE=[{placeId:"garching",captionKey:"tour.garching.campus",rangeM:1500,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"ubahn",captionKey:"tour.garching.ubahn",rangeM:700,holdMs:6e3},{placeId:"mw",captionKey:"tour.garching.mw",rangeM:600,holdMs:7e3},{placeId:"mi",captionKey:"tour.garching.mi",rangeM:600,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"frm2",captionKey:"tour.garching.frm2",rangeM:800,holdMs:6500}],KE={$comment:AE,id:RE,site:CE,lenses:NE,schedulerSite:DE,$schedulerSiteComment:LE,$lensesComment:UE,bbox:OE,shell:IE,workingCrs:PE,verticalDatum:kE,elevationRangeM:zE,verification:BE,drape:FE,grids:HE,shellGrids:GE,focusPlaces:VE,$focusPlacesComment:jE,rooms:WE,geobasis:$E,shellGeobasis:qE,roomsAttribution:XE,tour:YE},ZE="Area of interest definition for the Universität zu Köln — the sixth twin, and the FIRST built on Nordrhein-Westfalen geodata (PLAN §37). Köln is 3rd nationally at 47 238 students (DESTATIS GENESIS, WS 2024/25) and the largest university this project can reach: the two ahead of it are TU München and LMU, both already built. Getting here required a third survey authority, because NRW is where the German university system's mass actually sits — Köln, Aachen, Münster, Bochum, Duisburg-Essen and Bonn are all in this one state.",QE="koeln",JE={name:{de:"Universität zu Köln",en:"University of Cologne"},region:{de:"Köln, Nordrhein-Westfalen",en:"Cologne, North Rhine-Westphalia"},timezone:"Europe/Berlin"},e2=[],t2="Empty, deliberately — the same state OTH and FAU shipped in. A lens may only be declared where its data requirements can be met (`world.test.ts` enforces this). Köln publishes no timetable this project has access to, and no indoor geometry has been probed, so occupancy, staffing and quality are all impossible here. Declaring one anyway would produce a card that opens onto nothing, which this repo has shipped twice and does not intend to again.",n2={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:6.91,east:6.9406,south:50.9226,north:50.9373,$comment:"HIGH-RESOLUTION CORE, ~2.15 x 1.64 km. Taken from the campus cluster find_campus_areas.py resolved out of OpenStreetMap (config/campus-candidates.json, HS111: 11 areas around Albertus-Magnus-Platz) plus ~250 m of margin. This is the Lindenthal Hauptcampus — the Philosophikum, Hörsaalgebäude, Seminargebäude, Mensa and the science institutes along Zülpicher Straße. The medical campus and the outlying institutes are NOT in this box; Köln's second resolved cluster is a 40 x 10 m fragment and was not worth widening the AOI for."},i2={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:6.79,east:7.06,south:50.845,north:51.015,$comment:"COARSE TERRAIN SHELL, ~18.9 x 18.9 km. Holds the Rhine, the Innenstadt and the Ville ridge west of the city. ⚠️ Expect this shell to do LESS work than Tübingen's: the Cologne Bight is close to flat, so the horizon here is made of buildings rather than of terrain. The shell is still needed — without it the core would end in a cliff — but nobody will point at it."},a2="EPSG:25832",s2="DHHN2016",r2={min:35,max:75,$measured:!0,$comment:`MEASURED 2026-08-07 by build_terrain.py over the core: 40.42 .. 65.21 m, from 6 Geobasis NRW DGM1 tiles at 100% coverage (grid 1099 x 849 at 2 m). Left slightly loose around the measurement so a re-run after a NRW update does not trip the plausibility gate over a decimetre.

⚠️ 25 METRES OF RELIEF ACROSS THE WHOLE CORE — the flattest AOI in this repo by some distance (FAU 36 m, OTH ~78 m, Tübingen 127 m). The hypsometric ramp is doing almost nothing here and the terrain shading has nothing to shade; what makes this twin readable is the buildings and the drape. That is a fact about the Cologne Bight, not a defect in the build, and it is written down so nobody 'fixes' the terrain later.

Ground heights at the resolved focus places came out at Humanwissenschaftliche Fakultät 49.3 m and Köln Süd 55.4 m — plausible, and a second confirmation that the focus coordinates landed on the campus.`},o2={maxPx:4096,$comment:"Long side of the DOP mosaic, via the Geobasis NRW WMS (layer nw_dop_rgb, 10 cm source). NOT larger: at 8192 px the mipmap chain is ~300 MB, which Chromium accepts and then silently samples BLACK."},l2={sourceResolutionM:1,renderResolutionM:2,renderDecimation:2,$comment:"Geobasis NRW DGM1 source, resampled to a 2 m heightmap, mesh decimated 2x -> 4 m posting. The same tier as every other AOI here. ⚠️ Unlike Baden-Württemberg, NRW publishes DGM1 already as a float32 GeoTIFF with the ModelTiepoint/ModelPixelScale pair build_terrain.py reads, so there is no conversion step between the download and this grid."},c2={sourceResolutionM:30,renderResolutionM:30,renderDecimation:3,transitionBandM:250,$comment:"Copernicus GLO-30 -> ~90 m posting. transitionBandM is written in metres for readability but MUST be applied as a fraction of the core (CORE_FADE_FRACTION ~0.08), never absolute."},u2={probedOn:"2026-08-07",roomsFound:0,$comment:"⚠️ Named `indoorProbe` and NOT `rooms` — in this engine a `rooms` block MEANS real indoor geometry exists and drives the hero-building explode. Nothing has been found for Köln, so buildings stay solid and the app says so rather than inventing interiors."},d2=[{id:"hauptcampus",name:"Universität zu Köln",lat:50.92854,lon:6.92575},{id:"hoersaalgebaeude",name:"Hörsaalgebäude",lat:50.92707,lon:6.92779},{id:"philosophikum",name:"Philosophikum",lat:50.92797,lon:6.927},{id:"seminargebaeude",name:"Seminargebäude",lat:50.92689,lon:6.92715},{id:"mensa",name:"UniMensa",lat:50.9278,lon:6.93297},{id:"mathematik",name:"Mathematisches Institut",lat:50.92906,lon:6.92429},{id:"biozentrum",name:"Biozentrum Köln",lat:50.92682,lon:6.93624},{id:"cecad",name:"CECAD",lat:50.9255,lon:6.92035},{id:"geowissenschaften",name:"Geowissenschaften",lat:50.92693,lon:6.93466},{id:"humanwissenschaften",name:"Humanwissenschaftliche Fakultät",lat:50.93419,lon:6.91974},{id:"bahnhof",name:"Köln Süd",lat:50.9276,lon:6.93727,kind:"station"}],h2="Resolved 2026-08-07 from OpenStreetMap via Overpass BY TAG — `amenity=university`, `building=university`, university-operated buildings, libraries and stations inside the core box — and not by name, for the reason Tübingen's config records at length.\n\n⚠️ TWO DIFFERENT OSM RELATIONS ARE BOTH NAMED 'Universität zu Köln': relation/8727202 at 50.92854/6.92575, which is the Hauptcampus and is used above, and relation/1253808 at 50.92225/6.93468, roughly 600 m south-east. Picking by name alone is a coin toss between them. The one above was chosen because it sits inside the resolved campus cluster; the other is recorded here so the next person does not 'fix' it.",f2={authority:"Geobasis NRW (Bezirksregierung Köln)",licence:"Datenlizenz Deutschland – Zero – Version 2.0",licenceUrl:"https://www.govdata.de/dl-de/zero-2-0",attribution:"Datenquelle: Land NRW (Geobasis NRW), dl-de/zero-2-0",downloadBase:"https://www.opengeodata.nrw.de/produkte/geobasis/",dopWms:"https://www.wms.nrw.de/geobasis/wms_nw_dop",$comment:"The THIRD survey authority in this repo, after the Bavarian LDBV and Baden-Württemberg's LGL. pipeline.py's `in_nordrhein_westfalen` predicate keys on the string 'Geobasis NRW' here to select the NRW steps, so this field is load-bearing and not decoration.\n\n⚠️ dl-de/ZERO-2-0, not by-2-0: NRW places its geobasis data in the public domain and requires no attribution at all. The attribution is given anyway — every other source in this app is credited, and a licence that permits silence is not a reason to be silent about where a campus came from."},m2={authority:"ESA / DLR / Airbus Defence and Space — Copernicus DEM GLO-30",licence:"Copernicus DEM free licence (worldwide, free reuse with the prescribed notice)",licenceUrl:"https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM",attribution:"produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved",$attributionComment:"The ADAPTED-DATA form of the notice, which is prescribed rather than stylistic: the pipeline resamples the tile onto a UTM grid and shifts it onto the core's vertical datum.",cogUrlTemplate:"https://copernicus-dem-30m.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM.tif",tiles:["N50_E006","N50_E007","N51_E006","N51_E007"],$tilesComment:"FOUR tiles. The shell runs 50.845-51.015 N and 6.79-7.06 E, so it crosses BOTH the 51 N parallel and the 7 E meridian — the same four-corner case as OTH Regensburg. A missing tile does not raise an error; it renders as a flat shelf across that side of the horizon."},p2=[{placeId:"hauptcampus",captionKey:"tour.koeln.campus",rangeM:1e3,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"hoersaalgebaeude",captionKey:"tour.koeln.hoersaal",rangeM:450,holdMs:6e3},{placeId:"philosophikum",captionKey:"tour.koeln.philosophikum",rangeM:500,holdMs:6e3},{placeId:"biozentrum",captionKey:"tour.koeln.biozentrum",rangeM:600,holdMs:6e3}],g2={$comment:ZE,id:QE,site:JE,lenses:e2,$lensesComment:t2,bbox:n2,shell:i2,workingCrs:a2,verticalDatum:s2,elevationRangeM:r2,drape:o2,grids:l2,shellGrids:c2,indoorProbe:u2,focusPlaces:d2,$focusPlacesComment:h2,geobasis:f2,shellGeobasis:m2,tour:p2},v2="Area of interest for Campus-Scheduler, second site. Every coordinate and every count in this file was MEASURED via Overpass on 2026-07-31 by tools/geodata/probe_site.py — nothing here is recalled. Raw responses were written to temp/lmu-probe-*.json. The rule is inherited from Campus-Insights / Gleitschirm-Insights and was earned twice more here: no coordinate enters config without being looked up.",b2="lmu-muenchen",y2="2026-07-31",x2={name:{de:"LMU München",en:"LMU Munich"},region:{de:"München, Bayern",en:"Munich, Bavaria"},timezone:"Europe/Berlin"},_2="LMU HAS SIX SITES, AND THIS AOI DELIBERATELY HOLDS TWO OF THEM. A single-linkage clustering at 700 m over the 125 OSM features that name LMU (temp/lmu_cluster.py) returned: Stammgelände/Maxvorstadt 51 features (centre 48.15189/11.58054, 2284 x 1685 m); Campus Martinsried–Großhadern 30 features at 9.68 km; LMU Klinikum Campus Innenstadt 24 features at 2.61 km; Tierärztliche Fakultät Oberschleißheim 9 at 10.85 km; Universitäts-Sternwarte 5 at 1.98 km; Fakultät für Physik in Garching 2 at ~15 km. Stammgelände plus Klinikum Innenstadt is the pair that fits one photoreal core — and it is not a compromise, it is the same shape as the first customer: OTH's two campuses are 2.48 km apart, LMU's chosen two are 2.44 km apart. Martinsried, Oberschleißheim and Garching are recorded in `outOfCoreSites` below rather than silently dropped; they belong to the travel-time matrix long before they belong to the twin.",S2="⚠️ THE FIRST CLUSTERING FOUND A CAMPUS THAT DOES NOT EXIST. Matching /Ludwig-Maximilians|LMU/i against name and operator returned 227 features including a 14-feature 'campus' in Freiham — because 'lmu' is a substring of 'HeLMUt-Schmidt-Allee', 'HeLMUt-Karl-Platz' and 'Alois-WohLMUth-Straße'. With a word boundary the count is 125 and the phantom is gone. An acronym is a word, not a substring, and a case-insensitive three-letter match over a German street index will always find something.",w2=[{id:"stammgelaende",name:{de:"Stammgelände / Maxvorstadt",en:"Main campus / Maxvorstadt"},anchor:{lat:48.15049,lon:11.5798},anchorSource:"OSM way/82672176 amenity=university name='Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität' addr=Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1",bbox:{west:11.56,east:11.596,south:48.145,north:48.16},$bboxComment:"~2674 x 1663 m. MEASURED extent of the Hauptgebäude polygon (way/82672176, `out geom`) is only 235 x 301 m, and that is the point: unlike OTH, LMU's 'campus' is not a fenced site but an axis. The box spans from Luisenstraße 37 (Geowissenschaften, 11.5643) east to Oettingenstraße 67 (Informatik, 11.5944) and from Amalienstraße 17 (48.1470) north to Leopoldstraße 44 (48.1570), because those are where the measured LMU buildings are."},{id:"klinikum",name:{de:"Klinikum Campus Innenstadt",en:"University Hospital city campus"},anchor:{lat:48.13281,lon:11.56024},anchorSource:"OSM relation/6676202 amenity=university name='LMU Klinikum Campus Innenstadt'",bbox:{west:11.554,east:11.568,south:48.1275,north:48.138},$bboxComment:"~1040 x 1164 m. MEASURED extent of the campus outline (relation/6676202, `out geom`): west 11.55705, east 11.56343, south 48.12994, north 48.13567 = 473 x 638 m, plus ~250 m of margin so the Anatomische Anstalt (Pettenkoferstraße 11), the Institut für Humangenetik (Goethestraße 29) and the Pathologisches Institut (Thalkirchner Straße 36) all sit inside rather than on the edge. This one IS a real campus in the OTH sense: a contiguous clinical quarter with its own outline."}],M2={straightLineKm:2.44,$comment:"MEASURED between the two anchors above (haversine): 2.44 km — 1961 m north-south and 1453 m east-west. A second measurement between the two CLUSTER centroids gave 2.61 km. Note how close this is to OTH's 2.48 km: the demo's central constraint — a cohort cannot be in two places 40 minutes apart within one 15-minute break — transfers to LMU unchanged, and the travel-time matrix has to carry a real Munich U-Bahn/tram journey (U3/U6 Universität → Sendlinger Tor → Goetheplatz) rather than a straight line."},E2=[{id:"martinsried",name:"Campus Martinsried–Großhadern",lat:48.11236,lon:11.46428,distanceKm:9.68,features:30,note:"Biologie, Chemie/Pharmazie, Genzentrum, Klinikum Großhadern. The largest LMU site outside the core and the obvious phase-2 AOI."},{id:"oberschleissheim",name:"Tierärztliche Fakultät Oberschleißheim",lat:48.24703,lon:11.54779,distanceKm:10.85,features:9},{id:"garching-physik",name:"Fakultät für Physik, Garching",lat:48.26875,lon:11.67395,distanceKm:14.77,features:2,note:"OSM relation/16257718, Am Coulombwall 1 — inside the Campus-Insights Garching AOI, which is a different repository's site."},{id:"sternwarte",name:"Universitäts-Sternwarte",lat:48.14537,lon:11.60666,distanceKm:1.98,features:5,note:"Only 2 km out and just east of the core box. Included here rather than in the AOI because widening the core to reach it would add 1.5 km of Bogenhausen for one observatory."}],T2={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:11.554,east:11.596,south:48.1265,north:48.161,$comment:"PHOTOREAL CORE, ~3.12 x 3.83 km, covering BOTH campuses AND the corridor between them. Same rule as OTH: the corridor is not padding, it is the subject — the whole argument for a twin is that the inter-campus transition becomes visible. Roughly 1560 x 1915 samples at the 2 m grid below."},A2={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:11.45,east:11.7,south:48.05,north:48.24,$comment:"COARSE TERRAIN SHELL, ~18.6 x 21.1 km. Terrain only, fading into haze. ⚠️ Munich has almost nothing to put on its horizon: the Isar gravel plain rises about 60 m across the whole shell, so unlike Regensburg (Danube valley, Bayerischer-Wald foothills) this shell reads as a very slightly tilted plane. That is the truth about the site and the reason the registration gate leans on coverage rather than relief."},R2="EPSG:25832",C2="DHHN2016",N2={min:490,max:545,$measured:!0,$comment:"MEASURED 2026-07-31 by build_terrain.py over the core: 500.6 .. 532.8 m, from 25 LDBV DGM1 tiles at 100% coverage. The declared bracket is left deliberately loose around the measurement so a re-run after an LDBV data update does not trip the plausibility gate over a decimetre; uint16 quantisation over a 55 m bracket is ~0.8 mm, far finer than the source. CONSEQUENCE: just 32 m of relief across 3.8 km, against Regensburg's 78 m and closer to Garching's 12 m — terrain shading does almost no work here and the buildings carry the whole image. And unlike OTH, where the two campuses differ by 24 m and the walk between them is measurably downhill, LMU's two sites are 511.9 m (Hauptgebäude) and 520.2 m (Klinikum) — the Klinikum is 8 m HIGHER, which is within the noise of a city. The reason a cohort cannot cross between them is distance and the U-Bahn, not the terrain; do not reach for the OTH version of that story here."},D2={$comment:"Registration gate, composite form (Campus-Insights checks A-F). Munich has the opposite problem to the Alps and the same problem as Regensburg: an Overpass sweep of the core on 2026-07-31 returned 37 ele-tagged nodes and not one of them is a survey point. So registration is proven from coverage, plausibility, focus places, shell control points and the LDBV-vs-Copernicus seam offset.",minCoveragePct:99.5,toleranceM:3,shellToleranceM:12,maxSeamOffsetM:3,controlPoints:[{name:"Perlacher Mugl",lat:48.069204,lon:11.576829,publishedM:587,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/27236490 natural=peak ele=587 wikidata"},{name:"Baldehöhe",lat:48.065932,lon:11.509252,publishedM:580,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/7781604724 natural=peak ele=580"},{name:"Rodelberg Neuried",lat:48.077685,lon:11.498666,publishedM:574,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/12557739764 natural=peak ele=574"},{name:"Olympiaberg",lat:48.169852,lon:11.551629,publishedM:564,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/158712415 natural=peak ele=564 wikidata"},{name:"Fröttmaninger Berg",lat:48.21418,lon:11.630448,publishedM:562,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/263833045 natural=peak ele=562 wikidata"},{name:"Luitpoldhügel",lat:48.172422,lon:11.570897,publishedM:539,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/666304999 natural=peak ele=539 wikidata"},{name:"Hypoberg",lat:48.204514,lon:11.645326,publishedM:534,tier:"shell",source:"de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypoberg, 534 m ü. NHN, citing the Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung geoportal (v.bayern.de/JS56r). ⚠️ NOT the OSM value: node/331312920 carries ele=517, which is 17 m too low — see $hypobergCorrection."}],$controlPointsComment:`Seven named landforms, all in the shell, resolved from a sweep of 567 ele-tagged nodes. ⚠️ EVERY ONE OF THEM IS ARTIFICIAL. Munich is flat; each of these is a Schuttberg — wartime rubble (Olympiaberg, Luitpoldhügel, Hypoberg), a capped landfill (Fröttmaninger Berg) or a purpose-built toboggan mound (Perlacher Mugl, Rodelberg Neuried, Baldehöhe). That is not a defect for this purpose — a rubble hill with a surveyed summit is a perfectly good control point — but it does mean the whole set was created within living memory, so a survey epoch predating a raising or a landfill cap shows up as a one-sided error. It also means their PUBLISHED heights are less well curated than an Alpine summit's, which is exactly what went wrong here (see $hypobergCorrection).

MEASURED RESULT of the first run: six of the seven read BELOW their published value, by −0.43 to −7.68 m. That is the expected sign for a 30 m-posting radar model over a small steep mound — the summit is averaged away. A consistent negative bias of a physically explicable size is better evidence than a set that scatters.`,$hypobergCorrection:"⚠️ THE GATE CAUGHT A BAD PUBLISHED VALUE, AND THE MODEL WAS THE ONE TELLING THE TRUTH. First run: Hypoberg failed at +16.15 m against OSM's ele=517, the only point of the seven to read HIGH and by twice the largest deviation in either direction. Rather than widen shellToleranceM, the value was checked independently: the German Wikipedia article, citing the Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung geoportal, gives 534 m ü. NHN. The shell model reads 533.15 m — −0.85 m, in line with the other six both in sign and in size. So OSM's node is 17 m low and the registration was never in question. DO NOT restore 517, and DO NOT loosen the tolerance: the tolerance is what made this visible. Same class of event as OTH's Königswiesener Berg, opposite outcome — there two surveys contradicted OSM and the point was dropped; here an authority confirmed the model and the point was kept with a corrected reference.",$noCoreControlPoint:"There is NO control point inside the core, and that is a measured conclusion. The core contains 37 ele-tagged nodes: one named place node, one address node, and 35 cycle-route guideposts. All are rejected below. Garching and Regensburg are in the same position for the same reason, and the gate is designed for it: checks A, B, C and E carry the proof.",$rejectedCandidates:`Recorded so they are not silently re-added.

(1) node/1700534808 'München' (48.137108/11.575382, ele=519) — the CITY place node. It is the only named ele node inside the core and it is a label for a city of 1.5 million, not a point on the ground. Same class as the settlement nodes rejected for OTH (Kleinprüfening, Lappersdorf, Sinzing).

(2) The 35 cycle-network guideposts inside the core (e.g. node/4157038870 ele=515, node/4269745470 ele=553). ⚠️ These are more tempting than OTH's benches and bollards because they carry \`source:ele\`, i.e. somebody recorded where the number came from. They are still rejected: the value describes the signpost, the provenance behind \`source:ele\` is not stated per node, and a set of guideposts that disagree by 38 m over 1.5 km of pancake-flat Maxvorstadt (515 vs 553) cannot all be ground level. If a core control point is ever genuinely needed, this is where to look — after reading the source:ele values, not before.

(3) node/3712962532 (48.144601/11.561048, ele=492) — an ADDRESS node carrying an elevation. An address point is not a survey. Identical to OTH's rejected node/2251378676.

(4) node/6186388212 'Rockmuseum Munich' ele=693 — inside the Olympiaturm. That is a viewing platform 180 m up, and it is the highest 'elevation' in the whole sweep. Taking the maximum ele in a box is exactly how this one gets in.

(5) node/8221898808 'Windkraftanlage Freimann' ele=687 — a wind turbine; the value is hub height.

(6) node/5046900823 'Friedensmahnmal' ele=541 — a memorial standing ON the Luitpoldhügel (539, accepted above) at the same coordinate to five decimals. The 2 m difference is the monument. Two ele nodes at one spot means one of them is furniture.

(7) Settlement place nodes (Sauschütt 606, Taufkirchen 563, Unterhaching 556, Ottobrunn 555, Haar 542, Weideninsel 516, Karlsfeld 491, Dachau 482, Garching 482, Unterschleißheim 473) — village-centre labels with no defined ground point.

(8) node/13133380322 'Hoher Berg' 526 and node/667441727 'Rodelhügel Hochbrück' 490 — genuine landforms, but both lie NORTH of the shell box and were dropped for that reason alone. Widen the shell and they become candidates.`},L2={maxPx:4096,$built:"3381 x 4096 px at 0.96 m per pixel, 3.7 MB JPEG (measured 2026-07-31, one WMS request).",$comment:"Long side of the DOP20 mosaic → 0.96 m per pixel over the 3.94 km core, marginally coarser than OTH's 0.78 m because the box is longer. NOT larger: at 8192 px the mipmap chain is ~300 MB, which Chromium accepts and then silently samples BLACK. And the drape texture must be loaded with flipY=false and WITHOUT mipmaps (see PLAN §5.5)."},U2={sourceResolutionM:1,renderResolutionM:2,renderDecimation:2,$comment:"LDBV DGM1 source, resampled to a 2 m heightmap, mesh decimated 2x -> 4 m posting. Same tier as OTH and Garching. This core is ~37% larger in area than OTH's, so expect ~600k terrain vertices against ~450k."},O2={sourceResolutionM:30,renderResolutionM:30,renderDecimation:3,transitionBandM:250,$comment:"Copernicus GLO-30 -> ~90 m posting. transitionBandM is expressed here in metres for readability but MUST be applied as a fraction of the core (CORE_FADE_FRACTION ~0.08), never absolute — an absolute band tuned for a 9 km alpine AOI ate 43% of a 2 km campus and turned the drape into a dark blob."},I2={$comment:"HOW A BUILDING IS RECOGNISED AS LMU. This block exists because the OTH answer does not transfer. OTH occupies two fenced campuses, so point-in-polygon against its outlines is most of the answer. LMU is an urban university: its faculties stand in ordinary Maxvorstadt streets, next door to the Alte Pinakothek, the Bayerische Staatsbibliothek and — the real hazard — TUM's Stammgelände, 700 m west of LMU's Hauptgebäude. Proximity is worth even less here than it was in Regensburg, so the signals are ownership statements, not geometry.",outlineIds:["way/82672176","relation/6676202"],$outlineIdsComment:"Only two outlines exist and only one is a campus: relation/6676202 (Klinikum Campus Innenstadt, 473 x 638 m) is a real contiguous site, while way/82672176 is just the Hauptgebäude footprint (235 x 301 m). The outline test therefore catches a small minority of LMU buildings, which is why it is the weakest of the four signals here and was the strongest at OTH.",siteRelations:["relation/6441069"],$siteRelationsComment:"MEASURED: relation/6441069, tagged type=site + amenity=university + wikidata=Q55044, lists 75 members (68 ways, 4 relations, 3 nodes). 45 of them fall inside this core box and 52 of the 75 carry a building tag. This is an explicit statement of membership by the people who mapped it and it beats every geometric heuristic available over a city centre. ⚠️ It is also INCOMPLETE — see extraIds.",operatorPattern:"ludwig-maximilians",namePattern:"Ludwig-Maximilians|Ludwigs-Maximilians|(?<![A-Za-z])LMU(?![A-Za-z])",$namePatternComment:"The word-boundary form, for the reason in $regexLesson. 'Ludwigs-Maximilians' is not a typo in this file: way/832961760 is spelled that way in OSM and a strict pattern would drop it.",extraIds:["relation/116031"],$extraIdsComment:"⚠️ AN EXPLICIT ALLOW-LIST, WITH EVIDENCE, BECAUSE IT CARRIES THE BEST DATA ON THE SITE. relation/116031 is unnamed, has no operator tag and is not a member of the site relation, so all four signals miss it — and it holds 526 of the 952 mapped indoor rooms in the whole core. It is LMU's Institut für Informatik at Oettingenstraße 67: its centroid (48.15010/11.59440) matches the site relation's own member way/376680733 'Institut für Informatik der LMU' (48.15011/11.59441) to five decimal places, it is tagged building=university with 3 levels, and its room refs run A/C/D/E/F/G/H/L + three digits, which is the published Trakt scheme of Oettingenstraße 67. Four independent agreements. Anything added to this list must come with that much."},P2={measured:{osmBuildingsInCore:9435,osmWithBuildingLevels:4678,lod2BuildingsBuilt:15746,lod2Triangles:1100878,lod2AssetMB:18.9,$comment:"The OSM count (9435) was the PROBE, measured over a box 400 m narrower than the final core. The LDBV LoD2 build produced 15 746 buildings and 1 100 878 triangles from 9 CityGML tiles, having skipped 1217 structures under 18 m² and 24 900 outside the terrain extent. ⚠️ THE PROBE UNDERSTATED THE BUILD BY 67%, and the OTH numbers are why that was not expected: there the OSM probe said 8193 and the build produced 9105, an 11% gap, so 'OSM count ≈ LoD2 count' looked like a rule. It is not. LoD2 is a cadastral product that splits a Maxvorstadt block into its individual surveyed buildings where OSM maps the block as one outline, and the denser and older the fabric, the wider the two diverge. Do not size a new AOI from its OSM building count alone."},lodPolicy:{decision:"full LoD2 everywhere in the core",$comment:"⚠️ KEPT, BUT THE HEADROOM IS GONE — and this is the entry that was a forecast and has now been measured twice. Forecast (before the build, from the OTH outcome): 'a comparable building count, so expect a comparable ~8 MB'. Measured after the geodata pipeline: 18.90 MB of buildings and ~30.1 MB of browser assets. Measured again after the room geometry landed (rooms.json 2.25 MB + rooms.bin + occupancy.bin): **37.0 MB total**. That is 2.3x OTH's building payload and 1.8x its complete 20.2 MB set. It still ships — the inherited engine's own performance budget allows 34 MB for its larger site and 37 MB over Fabric static hosting is acceptable — but the corridor-LoD1 simplification that OTH forecast and never needed is now a REAL option, and this is the AOI that would have to write it. The next thing added to this scene should be paid for by simplifying the corridor, not by growing the budget again."}},k2={osmTrees:4746,osmTreeRows:120,osmLanduseAreas:671,cadastreTreesRendered:29580,$comment:"The OSM figures were the probe. The BUILD used the Bavarian tree cadastre (the München tile 124028_baeume.gpkg, 493 MB downloaded, cached and gitignored): 601 951 rows scanned, 567 488 outside the terrain, 4883 thinned, 29 580 trees kept at 9 m spacing in 0.27 MB of instance data. Heights 5.5–62.3 m, median 15.6 m. That is 6.2x what OSM knows about — a larger multiple than OTH saw (3.6x) and than Garching saw (7.4x), i.e. within the normal range for a city where street trees are surveyed but not mapped."},z2={measuredFootways:8037,measuredRoads:3586,measuredPtStops:73,measuredWater:143,$comment:"MEASURED 2026-07-31. Nearly twice OTH's footway count (4240) in a comparable area — this is a walkable inner city. ⚠️ Only 73 PT stops against OTH's 217, and that number is misleading rather than low: Munich's inner city moves on U-Bahn and S-Bahn, whose stations are mapped as stop areas and platforms below ground rather than as `highway=bus_stop` nodes. The travel-time matrix between the two campuses is a U-Bahn journey (Universität → Sendlinger Tor → Goetheplatz), so phase-4 routing must read railway stations here, not just the bus layer that was sufficient in Regensburg."},B2={$comment:"⚠️ THE HEADLINE NUMBER IS A TRAP AND THE ATTRIBUTED NUMBER IS THE FINDING. A plain query returns 952 `indoor=room` features inside the core — 33x what OTH has, and it would be very easy to write 'LMU is richly mapped indoors'. It is not. Joining every room to the building polygon that contains it (temp/lmu_indoor_owner.py, 10 713 outlines) shows the rooms belong overwhelmingly to TUM, whose Stammgelände sits inside any LMU Maxvorstadt box: Thierschbau, Gebäude R, Hochvolthaus, Verwaltungsbau, Mensa Arcisstraße and TUM's own Hauptgebäude account for ~185, and 182 rooms fall inside no building at all. This is the Universität-Regensburg problem from the OTH AOI, one order of magnitude worse, and the same rule applies: filter by ownership, never by proximity.",osmIndoorRoomsInCore:952,attributedToLmu:527,attributeToBuildings:!0,$attributeToBuildingsComment:"⚠️ MUST STAY TRUE HERE. It tells fetch_indoor_rooms.py to keep a mapped room only when its centroid falls inside a building the ownership test already accepted. OTH does not set it and does not need it — everything inside its campus boxes is OTH's. Munich is the opposite case and the flag is the whole difference between 527 rooms and 952.",$attributedComment:"MEASURED: 526 rooms in relation/116031 (Institut für Informatik, Oettingenstraße 67 — see ownership.extraIds for the four-way evidence that it is LMU) plus 1 in the Pathologisches Institut. Every other LMU building in the core has zero. So LMU's indoor data is not broad, it is ONE deeply mapped building — but that building has 19x the room count of OTH's Gebäude K (28) and three levels instead of one, which makes it a considerably better subject for the exploding-building view than the first customer had.",roomsByOwner:{"relation/116031 — LMU Institut für Informatik, Oettingenstraße 67":526,"relation/6758375 — TUM Verwaltungsbau":80,"way/19183732 — Mensa Arcisstraße (Studierendenwerk)":57,"way/97399424 — TUM Gebäude R":22,"way/61408163 — TUM Thierschbau":14,"way/10053349 — TUM Hauptgebäude":10,"way/158913000 — LMU Pathologisches Institut":1,"relation/52412 — Bayerische Staatsbibliothek":2,"(in no building outline)":182},codePattern:"^[A-Z] ?\\d{3}$",$codePatternComment:"DERIVED FROM REAL DATA, not invented: the mapped refs are 'A 001', 'A 105', 'C 111', 'L 102' — a single wing letter plus three digits. Measured prefix frequencies across the whole core: L 102, A 44, D 36, E 36, F 35, C 32, G 31, H 23. Those letters are the Trakte of Oettingenstraße 67, not a campus-wide building code, which is the opposite of OTH — where the letter identifies the BUILDING and the same pattern therefore means something different. Any Untis room list must be validated against the right interpretation.",buildingsWithLevelTags:{stammgelaende:2999,klinikum:529},$levelsComment:"Ways carrying building:levels (or indoor tags) in each campus box, and the reason generated floor plates are viable for the rest: floor COUNTS are real across the site even where floor PLANS are not."},F2=[{id:"hauptgebaeude",name:"LMU Hauptgebäude",lat:48.15049,lon:11.5798,source:"OSM way/82672176"},{id:"philologicum",name:"Philologicum",lat:48.14873,lon:11.57999,source:"OSM way/19322270"},{id:"mathematik",name:"Fakultät für Mathematik",lat:48.14811,lon:11.57284,source:"OSM way/165494491"},{id:"informatik",name:"Institut für Informatik (Oettingenstraße)",lat:48.15011,lon:11.59441,source:"OSM way/376680733"},{id:"amalienstrasse",name:"Fakultät für Informatik, Amalienstraße",lat:48.14702,lon:11.57592,source:"OSM way/115881074"},{id:"geowissenschaften",name:"Fakultät für Geowissenschaften",lat:48.14794,lon:11.56477,source:"OSM way/96114101"},{id:"palaeontologie",name:"Paläontologisches Museum",lat:48.14761,lon:11.56362,source:"OSM way/28026044"},{id:"tiermedizin",name:"Tierärztliche Fakultät",lat:48.14962,lon:11.58352,source:"OSM way/449701274"},{id:"psychologie",name:"Fakultät für Psychologie und Pädagogik",lat:48.15588,lon:11.58284,source:"OSM relation/52573"},{id:"klinikum",name:"LMU Klinikum Campus Innenstadt",lat:48.13281,lon:11.56024,source:"OSM relation/6676202"},{id:"anatomie",name:"Anatomische Anstalt",lat:48.13387,lon:11.55995,source:"OSM way/40151560"},{id:"pettenkofer",name:"Max von Pettenkofer-Institut",lat:48.13379,lon:11.56238,source:"OSM relation/1344490"},{id:"humangenetik",name:"Institut für Humangenetik",lat:48.13546,lon:11.55886,source:"OSM way/91908330"},{id:"pathologie",name:"Pathologisches Institut",lat:48.13003,lon:11.56496,source:"OSM way/158913000"}],H2="All fourteen resolved from the site relation and the Overpass probe on 2026-07-31 with their OSM ids recorded. A coordinate is only verified once something independent agrees with it — here that will be the terrain build sampling each place and the LoD2 footprints landing on them.",G2="⚠️ TUM'S STAMMGELÄNDE IS INSIDE THIS CORE BOX, roughly 700 m west of LMU's Hauptgebäude (Arcisstraße 21, around 48.1487/11.5679). It is a different university, it is larger than LMU on this map in terms of mapped interiors, and it must NEVER be presented as LMU. It will render, and it should: two of Germany's biggest universities sharing one district is the truth about Maxvorstadt and it makes the twin recognisable. It is also the single most likely source of a wrong number in this AOI — see indoorProbe, where an unfiltered count credits LMU with 952 rooms instead of 527. The Bayerische Staatsbibliothek, the Alte and Neue Pinakothek, the Glyptothek and the Bayerisches Nationalmuseum are inside the box for the same reason and with the same rule.",V2="The southern half of the core reaches the edge of the Altstadt ring at Sendlinger Tor and takes in the Theresienwiese approach to the west of the Klinikum. Good for the demo — the twin shows a city people recognise rather than a business park — and a reminder that this AOI, like OTH's, is a slice of a city rather than a campus.",j2=["occupancy","staffing","quality"],W2="lmu",$2={source:"tools/data/build_plan_quality.py — whole-cohort lecture days + slot desirability",studentGroupMappingModelled:!1},q2={source:"tools/data/build_staffing.py — course.sws joined to teacher.contractSws",lecturerTypesModelled:!1},X2="Declared only now that the data exists. The engine has a test — 'declares only lenses whose data requirements it can meet' — which failed the first OTH fork for declaring `occupancy` before the room data existed, so this stayed EMPTY until tools/data/build_room_geometry.py --site lmu had written rooms.json / rooms.bin / occupancy.bin. It now reports 9316 rooms, 520 of them from survey, and 130 rooms carrying bookings from the generated plan.",Y2={$comment:"Room-level analytics are possible here, and better founded than at the first site. Oettingenstraße 67 (relation/116031, the Institut für Informatik) carries 526 room outlines OpenStreetMap actually surveyed, across three levels — against OTH's 28 on one level of Gebäude K. Every other building's interior is generated: plates laid out inside the REAL footprint at the REAL storey count, badged `generated` on every record. Occupancy comes from the synthetic timetable rather than being invented separately, so the colour a room takes IS the plan the solver is working on.",codePattern:"^(?:[A-Z] ?)?U?\\d{3}[A-Z]?$",$codePatternComment:"MEASURED from the 526 refs, and wider than it looks because the survey itself is: 'A 001' and 'H 112' carry a wing letter, '075' and '179' do not, 'U167' is an Untergeschoss room, and '040A'/'U142A' carry a subdivision suffix. The OTH pattern (^[A-Z]{1,2} ?\\d{3}$) would reject the majority of them. ⚠️ Do NOT read the leading letter as a building: it is a Trakt of this one building.",osmRefKey:"ref",heroBuilding:"ax",heroBuildingOsmId:"relation/116031",$heroBuildingComment:"BOTH are recorded, and the OSM id is the one to trust. `ax` is the lower-case placeholder the generator assigned — lower case because this building is UNNAMED in OSM and the identifier is therefore ours, not LMU's — and it would change if the building list changed. The demo opens here because it is the only interior on the site that is real (520 of the 526 surveyed rooms, on three levels) and because it belongs to MIS, one of the two modelled faculties: the same double qualification Gebäude K has at OTH.",storeyHeightM:3.6,$storeyHeightComment:"ASSUMED. LoD2 gives building heights but not floor-to-floor pitch, and OSM has no level heights here. Slightly above OTH's 3.5 m because the measured Oettingenstraße refs run to three storeys in a building whose LoD2 height supports it. It is the weakest number in the interior and it is the one that shows: get it wrong and exploded floors interpenetrate.",levelProvenance:{$comment:"⚠️ MOST OF THESE FLOORS ARE DERIVED, NOT SURVEYED, and the split is recorded per room in `levelSource`. Only 32 of the 526 rooms carry an OSM `level` tag. The rest get their storey from the room number under the German convention (hundreds digit = storey, U prefix = Untergeschoss), which was CHECKED against those 32 and agreed with 32 of 32. Without it, 94% of the only real interior on this site would have been discarded and replaced by generated plates — the loss would have been silent, which is the part that matters.",taggedRooms:32,derivedFromRef:"the remainder",agreementOnTaggedRooms:"32 of 32"},referenceSemester:{id:"synthetic",startDate:"2026-10-13",endDate:"2027-02-05",$comment:"One representative teaching week from the generated plan, not a real semester. The start date is the Bavarian Wintersemester teaching start rather than OTH's 1 October, because LMU's lecture period begins in mid-October."}},K2={authority:"Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung (LDBV)",licence:"CC BY 4.0",licenceUrl:"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/deed.de",attribution:"Datenquelle: Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung – www.geodaten.bayern.de [Daten bearbeitet]",downloadBase:"https://download1.bayernwolke.de",downloadMirror:"https://download2.bayernwolke.de",metalinkBase:"https://geodaten.bayern.de/odd",$comment:"Identical to the OTH and Garching AOIs — München is in Bayern, so the same survey authority, the same portal and the same licence apply, and the pipeline needs no new fetcher (unlike Tübingen, which is Baden-Württemberg and required an LGL adapter). The attribution is not optional."},Z2={authority:"ESA / DLR / Airbus Defence and Space — Copernicus DEM GLO-30",licence:"Copernicus DEM free licence (worldwide, free reuse with the prescribed notice)",licenceUrl:"https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM",attribution:"produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved",$attributionComment:"The ADAPTED-DATA form of the notice, which is prescribed rather than stylistic: the pipeline resamples the tile onto a UTM grid and shifts it onto the core's vertical datum, so it is unambiguously modified.",cogUrlTemplate:"https://copernicus-dem-30m.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM.tif",tiles:["N48_E011"],$tilesComment:"ONE tile, unlike OTH's four: the shell spans 48.05–48.24 N and 11.45–11.70 E, so it crosses neither a parallel nor a meridian boundary. Worth stating explicitly because the OTH config warns about the opposite mistake — a missing tile shows up as a flat shelf on the horizon rather than as an error — and inheriting 'four tiles' here would download three empty ones."},Q2=[{placeId:"hauptgebaeude",captionKey:"tour.lmu.hauptgebaeude",rangeM:900,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"philologicum",captionKey:"tour.lmu.philologicum",rangeM:420,holdMs:5500},{placeId:"informatik",captionKey:"tour.lmu.informatik",rangeM:520,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"klinikum",captionKey:"tour.lmu.klinikum",rangeM:700,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"anatomie",captionKey:"tour.lmu.anatomie",rangeM:380,holdMs:5500}],J2="Five stops that tell the constraint rather than the architecture: the Hauptgebäude for scale, the Philologicum for the teaching stock, Oettingenstraße for the one building whose interior is real, then 2.4 km south to the Klinikum and its Anatomie — which is the moment the cohort's problem becomes visible.",eT={$comment:v2,id:b2,probedOn:y2,site:x2,$siteSelection:_2,$regexLesson:S2,campuses:w2,campusSeparation:M2,outOfCoreSites:E2,bbox:T2,shell:A2,workingCrs:R2,verticalDatum:C2,elevationRangeM:N2,verification:D2,drape:L2,grids:U2,shellGrids:O2,ownership:I2,buildings:P2,vegetation:k2,network:z2,indoorProbe:B2,focusPlaces:F2,$focusPlacesComment:H2,$neighbourNote:G2,$altstadtNote:V2,lenses:j2,schedulerSite:W2,planQuality:$2,staffing:q2,$lensesComment:X2,rooms:Y2,geobasis:K2,shellGeobasis:Z2,tour:Q2,$tourComment:J2},tT="Area of interest definition for the Universität Münster — 7th nationally at 41 962 students (DESTATIS GENESIS, WS 2024/25), and the third twin on the Nordrhein-Westfalen adapter.",nT="muenster",iT={name:{de:"Universität Münster",en:"University of Münster"},region:{de:"Münster, Nordrhein-Westfalen",en:"Münster, North Rhine-Westphalia"},timezone:"Europe/Berlin"},aT=[],sT="Empty, deliberately — a lens may only be declared where its data requirements can be met (`world.test.ts` enforces it). No timetable this project can read and no indoor survey, so occupancy, staffing and quality are impossible; `condition` would mean inventing a Sanierungsstau for a named real university.",rT={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:7.5885,east:7.6293,south:51.9572,north:51.9785,$comment:`HIGH-RESOLUTION CORE, ~2.80 x 2.37 km. From the campus cluster find_campus_areas.py resolved out of OpenStreetMap (config/campus-candidates.json, HS112: 31 areas) plus margin, widened slightly west so the Center for Soft Nanoscience at 7.59021 sits inside rather than exactly on the edge.

Like Aachen this holds two halves, and like Aachen that is the point: the Schlossplatz core in the east — the Fürstbischöfliches Schloss, the Hörsaalgebäude, the Universitäts- und Landesbibliothek — and the science campus along the Coesfelder Kreuz in the west (Physik, Chemie, Nanoscience). Münster's university is threaded through the city rather than fenced off, which is why the box is a box and not an outline.`},oT={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:7.471,east:7.747,south:51.883,north:52.053,$comment:"COARSE TERRAIN SHELL, ~18.9 x 18.9 km, over the Münsterland. ⚠️ Expect this shell to do even less work than Köln's: this is one of the flattest landscapes in Germany, so the horizon here is made of trees and buildings rather than of terrain. The shell still has to exist — without it the core would end in a cliff — but nobody will point at it."},lT="EPSG:25832",cT="DHHN2016",uT={min:45,max:85,$measured:!0,$comment:`MEASURED 2026-08-10 by build_terrain.py over the core: 50.70 .. 75.25 m, from 9 Geobasis NRW DGM1 tiles at 100% coverage (grid 1425 x 1212 at 2 m). Left slightly loose so a re-run after an NRW update does not trip the plausibility gate over a decimetre.

⚠️ 24.5 METRES ACROSS THE WHOLE CORE — the flattest AOI in this repo, narrowly under Köln's 25 m. The hypsometric ramp and the terrain shading have almost nothing to work with here; what makes this twin readable is the buildings, the drape and the trees. That is the Münsterland, not a broken build, and it is written down so nobody 'fixes' the terrain later. The starting guess of 40-110 was nearly three times the real spread.`},dT={maxPx:4096,$comment:"Long side of the DOP mosaic, via the Geobasis NRW WMS (layer nw_dop_rgb, 10 cm source). NOT larger: at 8192 px the mipmap chain is ~300 MB, which Chromium accepts and then silently samples BLACK."},hT={sourceResolutionM:1,renderResolutionM:2,renderDecimation:2,$comment:"Geobasis NRW DGM1, resampled to a 2 m heightmap, mesh decimated 2x -> 4 m posting — the same tier as every other AOI here."},fT={sourceResolutionM:30,renderResolutionM:30,renderDecimation:3,transitionBandM:250,$comment:"Copernicus GLO-30 -> ~90 m posting. transitionBandM is written in metres for readability but MUST be applied as a fraction of the core (CORE_FADE_FRACTION ~0.08), never absolute."},mT={probedOn:"2026-08-10",roomsFound:0,$comment:"⚠️ Named `indoorProbe` and NOT `rooms` — a `rooms` block MEANS real indoor geometry exists and drives the hero-building explode. Nothing probed here, so buildings stay solid and the app says so rather than inventing interiors."},pT=[{id:"schloss",name:"Fürstbischöfliches Schloss",lat:51.96361,lon:7.6133},{id:"hoersaalgebaeude",name:"Hörsaalgebäude Schlossplatz",lat:51.96266,lon:7.61828},{id:"ulb",name:"Universitäts- und Landesbibliothek",lat:51.96283,lon:7.6209},{id:"alte_ub",name:"Alte Universitätsbibliothek",lat:51.96105,lon:7.62123},{id:"botanicum",name:"Botanicum",lat:51.96312,lon:7.61061},{id:"englisches_seminar",name:"Englisches Seminar",lat:51.96137,lon:7.62273},{id:"it_center",name:"Center for Information Technology",lat:51.96605,lon:7.60381},{id:"mathematik",name:"Bibliothek Mathematik",lat:51.96583,lon:7.60273},{id:"physik",name:"Angewandte Physik",lat:51.96563,lon:7.5993},{id:"chemie",name:"Anorganische und Analytische Chemie",lat:51.968,lon:7.59785},{id:"nanoscience",name:"Center for Soft Nanoscience",lat:51.96925,lon:7.59021},{id:"sport",name:"Institut für Sportwissenschaft",lat:51.97206,lon:7.59915}],gT="Resolved 2026-08-10 from OpenStreetMap via Overpass BY TAG AND OPERATOR, not by remembered name — the discipline Tübingen's config argues for at length.\n\n⚠️ THE UNIVERSITY'S MAIN BUILDING IS A BAROQUE PALACE, AND THAT IS NOT A MISTAKE IN THE DATA. `way/13742054` is tagged `amenity=university`, `operator=Universität Münster` and named *Fürstbischöfliches Schloss* — the prince-bishops' residence, which has housed the Rektorat since 1954. A reader checking the twin against a mental model of 'university buildings' would be right to query it and wrong to change it.\n\n⚠️ Also filtered OUT deliberately: `Bereichsbibliothek Hüfferstiftung` (way/135451580) sits inside this box and carries `operator=Fachhochschule Münster` — a DIFFERENT institution sharing the city. Same trap as TU München inside the LMU core box, and the reason the query asks for the operator rather than trusting proximity.",vT={authority:"Geobasis NRW (Bezirksregierung Köln)",licence:"Datenlizenz Deutschland – Zero – Version 2.0",licenceUrl:"https://www.govdata.de/dl-de/zero-2-0",attribution:"Datenquelle: Land NRW (Geobasis NRW), dl-de/zero-2-0",downloadBase:"https://www.opengeodata.nrw.de/produkte/geobasis/",dopWms:"https://www.wms.nrw.de/geobasis/wms_nw_dop",$comment:"pipeline.py's `in_nordrhein_westfalen` predicate keys on the string 'Geobasis NRW' here, so this field is load-bearing. The authority is named for the whole state despite sitting in Cologne's Bezirksregierung — that is how NRW publishes it."},bT={authority:"ESA / DLR / Airbus Defence and Space — Copernicus DEM GLO-30",licence:"Copernicus DEM free licence (worldwide, free reuse with the prescribed notice)",licenceUrl:"https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM",attribution:"produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved",$attributionComment:"The ADAPTED-DATA form of the notice, which is prescribed rather than stylistic: the pipeline resamples the tile onto a UTM grid and shifts it onto the core's vertical datum.",cogUrlTemplate:"https://copernicus-dem-30m.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM.tif",tiles:["N51_E007","N52_E007"],$tilesComment:"TWO tiles. The shell runs 51.883-52.053 N, so it crosses the 52 N parallel; longitude stays inside E007 throughout. A missing tile does not raise an error — it renders as a flat shelf across the northern horizon."},yT=[{placeId:"schloss",captionKey:"tour.muenster.schloss",rangeM:800,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"hoersaalgebaeude",captionKey:"tour.muenster.hoersaal",rangeM:500,holdMs:6e3},{placeId:"ulb",captionKey:"tour.muenster.bibliothek",rangeM:500,holdMs:6e3},{placeId:"nanoscience",captionKey:"tour.muenster.naturwissenschaften",rangeM:900,holdMs:6e3}],xT={$comment:tT,id:nT,site:iT,lenses:aT,$lensesComment:sT,bbox:rT,shell:oT,workingCrs:lT,verticalDatum:cT,elevationRangeM:uT,drape:dT,grids:hT,shellGrids:fT,indoorProbe:mT,focusPlaces:pT,$focusPlacesComment:gT,geobasis:vT,shellGeobasis:bT,tour:yT},_T="Area of interest for Campus-Scheduler. Every coordinate and every count in this file was MEASURED via Overpass on 2026-07-30 by tools/geodata/probe_oth.py — nothing here is recalled. Raw responses were written to temp/oth-probe-*.json. The rule is inherited from Campus-Insights / Gleitschirm-Insights: no coordinate enters config without being looked up, because an earlier project shipped an AOI built around a place node 4.6 km from the town it named.",ST="oth-regensburg",wT="2026-07-30",MT={name:{de:"OTH Regensburg",en:"OTH Regensburg"},region:{de:"Regensburg, Bayern",en:"Regensburg, Bavaria"},timezone:"Europe/Berlin"},ET=[{id:"seyboth",name:{de:"Campus Seybothstraße / Galgenberg",en:"Seybothstraße / Galgenberg campus"},anchor:{lat:49.00308,lon:12.09627},anchorSource:"OSM way/28938080 amenity=university name='Ostbayerische Technische Hochschule Regensburg' addr=Seybothstraße 2",bbox:{west:12.09,east:12.1015,south:49,north:49.007},$bboxComment:"~840 x 780 m. MEASURED extent of the campus polygon (OSM way/28938080, `out geom`): west 12.09331, east 12.09923, south 49.00202, north 49.00413 = 432 x 234 m. The box adds ~250 m of margin so the Seybothstraße frontage, the Galgenbergstraße faculty buildings and the OTH relation/1623803 node (49.00458, just north of the polygon) all sit inside rather than on the edge."},{id:"pruefening",name:{de:"Campus Prüfeninger Straße",en:"Prüfeninger Straße campus"},anchor:{lat:49.01742,lon:12.07024},anchorSource:"OSM relation/1733231 amenity=university name='Ostbayerische Technische Hochschule Regensburg'",bbox:{west:12.0655,east:12.075,south:49.0142,north:49.0207},$bboxComment:"~695 x 723 m. MEASURED extent of the campus polygon (OSM relation/1733231, `out geom`): west 12.06933, east 12.07116, south 49.01639, north 49.01845 = 134 x 230 m — a much smaller site than Seybothstraße. The box is that polygon plus ~250 m of margin, the same rule as campus A. ⚠️ 134 m of frontage is suspiciously narrow for a whole campus: OSM's outline here is probably partial, so re-check against the LoD2 footprints once they are built and widen if buildings fall outside."}],TT={straightLineKm:2.48,$comment:"MEASURED between the two anchors above (haversine): 2.48 km. A second measurement between the OTH Regensburg node (49.00447/12.09331) and the Prüfening car park (49.01668/12.06982) gave 2.19 km. ⚠️ CORRECTION TO AN ASSUMPTION: the plan originally carried '~4-5 km' from the customer conversation. The two campuses are roughly HALF that apart in a straight line. Walking/PT distance will be longer (Regensburg street network, no direct line), and that is the number the travel-time matrix must actually use — measure it in phase 4 rather than inflating the straight line.",pairsM:{"seyboth-pruefening":2479,"seyboth-techbase":305,"pruefening-techbase":2760},$pairsComment:"MEASURED between the anchors (haversine, 2026-08-03). ⚠️ THE THIRD SITE BREAKS THE 'DIFFERENT CAMPUS MEANS BUS' SHORTHAND. Seybothstraße to TechBase is 305 m — under four minutes on foot — while Seybothstraße to Prüfening is 2.5 km and has always been modelled as a bus. So a transfer must be judged by DISTANCE, not by whether the campus id changed. `build_walk_routes.py --matrix` already picks the quicker of walk and transit per pair, which is why it gets this right; the straight-line fallback in `generate_timetable.py` was campus-based and had to be fixed to match."},AT={$comment:"How an OTH building is recognised. Stated explicitly rather than left to the default, because the default derives `outlineIds` from every campus `anchorSource` — and TechBase's anchor is a BUILDING outline, not a campus outline, so the default would have silently turned 'inside TechBase's own footprint' into an ownership test.",outlineIds:["way/28938080","relation/1733231"],$outlineComment:"The two real campus polygons only: Seybothstraße 2 and Prüfeninger Straße. TechBase is deliberately NOT here.",operatorPattern:"ostbayerische technische hochschule",extraIds:["relation/5747922"],$extraComment:"⚠️ TechBase Regensburg, claimed by hand and only by hand. No general signal reaches it and none should: the building is `building=office` operated by TechBase Regensburg, and OTH is one tenant among Vector Informatik, GEFASOFT, intive and Sensorik-Bayern. What justifies the entry is OSM node/4149309792 — the Sensorik-Applikationszentrum, `operator=Ostbayerische Technische Hochschule Regensburg`, at Franz-Mayer-Straße 1 — which is OTH's own statement that it operates there. The allow-list is the right instrument precisely because this is a tenancy and a rule that generalised it would start pulling in the neighbours."},RT={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:12.062,east:12.104,south:48.9985,north:49.024,$comment:"PHOTOREAL CORE, ~3.07 x 2.84 km, covering BOTH campuses AND the corridor between them. The corridor is not padding: the whole point of the twin is to make the inter-campus transition visible, so the ground between the two sites has to be rendered, not implied. Roughly 1535 x 1420 samples at the 2 m grid below."},CT={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:11.98,east:12.2,south:48.93,north:49.1,$comment:"COARSE TERRAIN SHELL, ~16 x 19 km. Terrain only, fading into haze. Unlike Garching this shell has something to show: the Danube valley to the north and the Bayerischer-Wald foothills to the east give the horizon real shape."},NT="EPSG:25832",DT="DHHN2016",LT={min:320,max:430,$measured:!0,$comment:"MEASURED 2026-07-30 by build_terrain.py over the core: 328.0 .. 405.5 m, from 20 LDBV DGM1 tiles at 100% coverage. The declared bracket is left deliberately loose around the measurement so a re-run after an LDBV data update does not trip the plausibility gate over a decimetre; uint16 quantisation over a 110 m bracket is ~1.7 mm, far finer than the source. CONSEQUENCE: ~78 m of relief across the core against Garching's 20 m, so terrain shading does real work here. And the two campuses are NOT on the same level — Seybothstraße sits at ~365 m, Prüfening at 341 m (both sampled from the built terrain). The walk between them is 2.5 km AND 24 m downhill, which is a better answer to 'why can't the cohort just walk?' than a flat distance."},UT={$comment:"Registration gate, composite form (Campus-Insights checks A-F). The Alpine strategy of >=5 published summits is impossible here: an Overpass probe of the core on 2026-07-30 returned exactly TWO ele-tagged nodes in 3 x 2.8 km of city. So registration is proven from coverage, plausibility, focus places, control points and the LDBV-vs-Copernicus seam offset instead.",minCoveragePct:99.5,toleranceM:3,shellToleranceM:12,maxSeamOffsetM:3,controlPoints:[{name:"Ziegetsberg",lat:48.990092,lon:12.06664,publishedM:440,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/1068928848 natural=peak ele=440"},{name:"Sallerner Berg",lat:49.042046,lon:12.107486,publishedM:390,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/356304449 natural=peak ele=390"},{name:"Hoher Sand",lat:49.05444,lon:12.078738,publishedM:400,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/1068890655 natural=peak ele=400"},{name:"Eichelberg",lat:49.065924,lon:12.072945,publishedM:420,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/1068890653 natural=peak ele=420"},{name:"Mühlberg",lat:49.054818,lon:12.11269,publishedM:408,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/1068936853 natural=peak ele=408"},{name:"Winzerer Höhe",lat:49.037703,lon:12.049844,publishedM:440,tier:"shell",source:"OSM node/1068931236 natural=peak ele=440"}],$controlPointsComment:"Resolved 2026-07-30 from an Overpass sweep for ele-tagged nodes, then VERIFIED against the built terrain. All six are named landforms around the Danube valley and all six pass at shell tolerance, reading +0.94 to +8.44 m above published — a consistent POSITIVE bias, which is exactly what a radar SURFACE model should do over vegetated ground. A set of control points that all err in the same direction by a physically explicable amount is better evidence than a set that scatters.",$noCoreControlPoint:"There is NO control point inside the core, and that is a measured conclusion rather than laziness. The core contains exactly two ele-tagged OSM nodes; one is an address node (rejected below) and the other, 'Königswiesener Berg', was TESTED AND REJECTED — see $rejectedCandidates. Garching's AOI is in the same position for the same reason, and the gate is designed for it: checks A, B, C and E carry the proof.",$rejectedCandidates:`Recorded so they are not silently re-added.

(1) node/3544035334 'Königswiesener Berg' (49.007556/12.069562, natural=peak, ele=397) — the ONLY peak inside the core, and it FAILED the gate by -14.21 m. Investigated rather than deleted or excused: the LDBV DGM1 bare-earth model reads 382.82 m at the node and never exceeds 386.11 m ANYWHERE within 600 m of it, while the independent Copernicus radar SURFACE model reads 384.20 m at the node with a local maximum of 390.33 m. Two surveys — different sensors, different decades, different datums — agree with each other and disagree with OSM, and the canopy hypothesis does not rescue it either (only ~1.4 m of surface-minus-ground at the node). The published 397 m is therefore not supported by any measurement available here. ⚠️ DO NOT loosen \`toleranceM\` to make this pass: the tolerance is what makes the gate mean something, and this is the gate working.

(2) node/2251378676 'Lydia Goldmann' (49.015352/12.100334, ele=343) — an ADDRESS node (addr:city/housenumber/postcode) that happens to carry an elevation. An address point is not a survey.

(3) Benches (node/1242346088, node/1242346094, ele=449.0/449.5), a bollard (node/1222078669, ele=381.00) and other amenity nodes — GPS-tagged street furniture.

(4) Settlement \`place\` nodes (Kleinprüfening 336, Lappersdorf 344, Sinzing 355 …) — village-centre labels with no defined ground point.`},OT={maxPx:4096,$built:"4096 x 3806 px at 0.78 m per pixel, 3.3 MB JPEG (measured 2026-07-30).",$comment:"Long side of the DOP20 mosaic. NOT larger: at 8192 px the mipmap chain is ~300 MB, which Chromium accepts and then silently samples BLACK. And the drape texture must be loaded with flipY=false and WITHOUT mipmaps (see PLAN §5.5)."},IT={sourceResolutionM:1,renderResolutionM:2,renderDecimation:2,$comment:"LDBV DGM1 source, resampled to a 2 m heightmap, mesh decimated 2x -> 4 m posting. Same tier as Garching; the AOI is only ~20% wider so the vertex budget is comparable (~450k)."},PT={sourceResolutionM:30,renderResolutionM:30,renderDecimation:3,transitionBandM:250,$comment:"Copernicus GLO-30 -> ~90 m posting. transitionBandM is expressed here in metres for readability but MUST be applied as a fraction of the core (CORE_FADE_FRACTION ~0.08), never absolute — an absolute band tuned for a 9 km alpine AOI ate 43% of a 2 km campus and turned the drape into a dark blob."},kT={measured:{osmBuildingsInCore:8193,osmWithBuildingLevels:4675,lod2BuildingsBuilt:9105,lod2Triangles:483982,lod2AssetMB:8.31,$comment:"The OSM count (8 193) was the PROBE; the LDBV LoD2 build produced 9 105 buildings and 483 982 triangles from 9 CityGML tiles. LoD2 is the authoritative cadastral source and legitimately holds buildings OSM has not mapped, so the higher number is expected rather than alarming. Either way this is an order of magnitude past Garching, whose whole core held 263."},lodPolicy:{decision:"full LoD2 everywhere in the core",$comment:"⚠✅ THE PLANNED LoD1-CORRIDOR SPLIT TURNED OUT TO BE UNNECESSARY, and the plan said to measure before deciding. Forecast: 8 193 buildings at full LoD2 would blow a ~10 MB asset budget, so the corridor should drop to LoD1 box extrusion. Measurement: all 9 105 buildings at full LoD2 come to 8.31 MB, and the complete asset set (terrain, shell, drape, land cover, vegetation, buildings) to 20.2 MB. That is roughly twice Campus-Insights' 9.4 MB and entirely acceptable over Fabric static hosting. So the corridor keeps its real roof shapes, the Altstadt reads as the Altstadt, and a whole simplification code path was never written. Revisit only if the asset set grows past ~30 MB."}},zT={osmTrees:6078,osmTreeRows:29,osmLanduseAreas:1139,cadastreTreesRendered:21681,$comment:"The OSM figures were the probe. The BUILD used the Bavarian tree cadastre (two Oberpfalz tiles, ~1.04 GB downloaded, cached and gitignored) and kept 21 681 trees at 9 m spacing — 3.6x what OSM knows about, in 0.20 MB of instance data. Same multiple Garching saw (14 081 cadastre vs 1 905 OSM)."},BT={measuredFootways:4240,measuredRoads:2638,measuredPtStops:217,measuredWater:75,$comment:"MEASURED 2026-07-30. This is the network the phase-4 real-routing step will run on: 4240 footway/path/cycleway segments and 217 PT stops between the two campuses is more than enough to compute an honest walking + public-transport travel time instead of a straight-line guess."},FT={$comment:"⚠️ NOT a `rooms` block — deliberately. In this engine the presence of `rooms` MEANS 'this site has real indoor data', and OTH does not. This block records what the probe FOUND, so the absence is documented rather than merely empty. PLAN §5.4: OSM indoor mapping for OTH is effectively absent — 29 `indoor=room` features in the Seybothstraße core, all on level 0 of a single building, and ZERO at Prüfening. (Garching, for contrast, has ~2800 rooms carrying ref:tum plus the NavigaTUM API.) There is no NavigaTUM equivalent for OTH. => the twin runs on OTH floor plans if OTH provides them, otherwise on floor plates generated from the Untis room list, badged as derived. A `rooms` block appears here only when real geometry does.",osmIndoorRooms:{seyboth:29,pruefening:0},codePattern:"^[A-Z]{1,2} ?\\d{3}$",$codePatternComment:"DERIVED FROM REAL DATA, not invented: the 29 mapped rooms carry refs of the form 'K 001', 'K 017', with names like 'K 001 Großer Hörsaal' and 'K 006 CIP-Pool'. So an OTH room code is a building letter plus a three-digit number — a different shape from TUM's 5606.EG.041, and the pattern the Untis room list should be validated against.",buildingsWithLevelTags:{seyboth:452,pruefening:696},$levelsComment:"Ways carrying building:levels (or indoor tags) in each campus box. This is what makes option 2 viable: floor COUNTS are real even though floor PLANS are not, so generated floor plates sit at the right heights and the right number of storeys."},HT=[{id:"oth",name:"OTH Regensburg",lat:49.0045,lon:12.09333,source:"OSM relation/1623803"},{id:"hoersaal",name:"Hörsaalgebäude",lat:49.00372,lon:12.09518,source:"OSM way/472818195"},{id:"bibliothek",name:"Hochschulbibliothek",lat:49.00309,lon:12.09597,source:"OSM way/29153707"},{id:"seminar",name:"Seminargebäude",lat:49.00334,lon:12.09423,source:"OSM relation/59800"},{id:"maschinenbau",name:"Fakultät Maschinenbau",lat:49.00327,lon:12.09792,source:"OSM relation/59801"},{id:"informatik",name:"Fakultät Informatik und Mathematik",lat:49.00242,lon:12.0975,source:"OSM relation/18374230"},{id:"architektur",name:"Fakultät Architektur",lat:49.00246,lon:12.09847,source:"OSM way/728790520"},{id:"elektrotechnik",name:"Laborgebäude Elektrotechnik",lat:49.00281,lon:12.09463,source:"OSM way/29153704"},{id:"mikrosystemtechnik",name:"Laborgebäude Mikrosystemtechnik",lat:49.00273,lon:12.0938,source:"OSM way/240509245"},{id:"forum",name:"Hörsaalgebäude am Forum",lat:49.00291,lon:12.0975,source:"OSM way/132014702"},{id:"pruefening",name:"Campus Prüfeninger Straße",lat:49.01742,lon:12.07024,source:"OSM relation/1733231"}],GT="All eleven resolved from the Overpass probe on 2026-07-30 with their OSM ids recorded. A coordinate is only verified once something independent agrees with it — here that will be the terrain build sampling each place and the LoD2 footprints landing on them.",VT="Universität Regensburg (OSM relation/6576273, centre 48.99653/12.09615) sits IMMEDIATELY south of the Seybothstraße campus. Its centre falls just outside the core box (south of 48.9985) but its northern buildings — e.g. 'SGLG Sammelgebäude' at 48.99888/12.09312 — are inside it, so UR WILL be rendered. It is a different institution and must never be presented as OTH: useful context in the render, a trap in the data. Filter by the OTH relations, never by proximity.",jT="Because the core spans both campuses AND the corridor, it also contains the Regensburg Altstadt, the Dom and the Danube — confirmed by a unit test that failed when the cathedral was used as an out-of-AOI reference point. Good for the demo (the twin shows a UNESCO old town, not an anonymous business park) and a reminder that this AOI is a slice of a city rather than a campus.",WT=["occupancy","staffing","quality"],$T="⚠️ OTH's OWN UNTIS EXPORT IS THE DEFAULT, not the generated plan. Decided 2026-08-06: showing the customer their real week is a stronger demo than showing them ours, and the buildings, terrain and walking routes are identical either way because it is the same campus. The generated dataset is still built, still served (site 'oth') and still what every e2e spec pins — they pass '?scheduler=oth' explicitly rather than inheriting whatever the default happens to be. See PLAN §25 and §27.",qT="oth-real",XT={source:"tools/data/build_plan_quality.py — whole-cohort lecture days + slot desirability",studentGroupMappingModelled:!1},YT={source:"tools/data/build_staffing.py — course.sws joined to teacher.contractSws",lecturerTypesModelled:!1},KT="`occupancy` is declared because the data to support it now EXISTS — tools/data/build_room_geometry.py writes rooms.json/rooms.bin/occupancy.bin, with Gebäude K's ground floor as surveyed OSM outlines and every other floor as plates laid out inside the real building footprint. It was deliberately EMPTY before that, and the engine's own test ('declares only lenses whose data requirements it can meet') failed the first attempt to declare it early. `flow` stays off until cohort movement is built.",ZT={$comment:"Room-level analytics are possible here, but only partly from survey. Gebäude K, Ebene 0 = 28 rooms OpenStreetMap actually mapped, with real outlines, areas and names. Everything else = generated plates inside the real footprint at the real storey count: right number, right area, right floor, arranged rather than surveyed, and badged `generated` on every record. Occupancy comes from the synthetic timetable rather than being invented separately, so the colour a room takes IS the plan the solver is working on.",codePattern:"^[A-Za-z]{1,2} ?\\d{3}$",osmRefKey:"ref",heroBuilding:"K",$heroBuildingComment:"The demo opens on K because it is the only building whose interior is real — and it happens to be the Fakultät Informatik und Mathematik, one of the two faculties modelled. K 001 Großer Hörsaal (105 m²) and the two CIP-Pools are surveyed rooms, not props.",storeyHeightM:3.5,$storeyHeightComment:"ASSUMED. LoD2 gives building heights but not floor-to-floor pitch, and OSM has no level heights for these buildings. It is the weakest number in the interior and it is the one that shows: get it wrong and exploded floors interpenetrate.",referenceSemester:{id:"synthetic",startDate:"2026-10-01",endDate:"2027-02-05",$comment:"One representative teaching week from the generated plan, not a real semester."}},QT={authority:"Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung (LDBV)",licence:"CC BY 4.0",licenceUrl:"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/deed.de",attribution:"Datenquelle: Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung – www.geodaten.bayern.de [Daten bearbeitet]",downloadBase:"https://download1.bayernwolke.de",downloadMirror:"https://download2.bayernwolke.de",metalinkBase:"https://geodaten.bayern.de/odd",$comment:"Identical to the Garching AOI — Regensburg is in Bayern, so the same survey authority, the same portal and the same licence apply. This is why the pipeline needed no new fetcher (unlike Tübingen, which is Baden-Württemberg and required an LGL adapter). The attribution is not optional."},JT={authority:"ESA / DLR / Airbus Defence and Space — Copernicus DEM GLO-30",licence:"Copernicus DEM free licence (worldwide, free reuse with the prescribed notice)",licenceUrl:"https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM",attribution:"produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved",$attributionComment:"The ADAPTED-DATA form of the notice, which is prescribed rather than stylistic: the pipeline resamples the tile onto a UTM grid and shifts it onto the core's vertical datum, so it is unambiguously modified.",cogUrlTemplate:"https://copernicus-dem-30m.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM.tif",tiles:["N48_E011","N48_E012","N49_E011","N49_E012"],$tilesComment:"FOUR tiles, not one: the shell spans 48.93-49.10 N and 11.98-12.20 E, so it crosses BOTH the 49 N parallel and the 12 E meridian. Garching needed a single tile and it would be easy to inherit that assumption — a missing N49 tile shows up as a flat shelf across the northern horizon, not as an error."},eA=[{placeId:"oth",captionKey:"tour.oth.campus",rangeM:1200,holdMs:6500},{placeId:"hoersaal",captionKey:"tour.oth.hoersaal",rangeM:450,holdMs:6e3},{placeId:"informatik",captionKey:"tour.oth.informatik",rangeM:500,holdMs:6e3},{placeId:"pruefening",captionKey:"tour.oth.pruefening",rangeM:900,holdMs:7e3}],tA="Ends at Prüfening on purpose: the last thing the viewer should see is the OTHER campus, 2.48 km away, because that distance is the constraint the whole product exists to handle.",nA={$comment:_T,id:ST,probedOn:wT,site:MT,campuses:ET,campusSeparation:TT,ownership:AT,bbox:RT,shell:CT,workingCrs:NT,verticalDatum:DT,elevationRangeM:LT,verification:UT,drape:OT,grids:IT,shellGrids:PT,buildings:kT,vegetation:zT,network:BT,indoorProbe:FT,focusPlaces:HT,$focusPlacesComment:GT,$neighbourNote:VT,$altstadtNote:jT,lenses:WT,$schedulerSiteComment:$T,schedulerSite:qT,planQuality:XT,staffing:YT,$lensesComment:KT,rooms:ZT,geobasis:QT,shellGeobasis:JT,tour:eA,$tourComment:tA},iA="Area of interest definition. The second instance, and the one that proves the engine is not welded to Bavaria: every geobasis source below is a different authority with a different portal (LGL Baden-Württemberg instead of LDBV). See NOTICE.md for the attribution each survey requires.",aA="tuebingen",sA={name:{de:"Universität Tübingen — Altstadt & Neckarfront",en:"University of Tübingen — Old Town & Neckar Front"},region:{de:"Tübingen, Baden-Württemberg",en:"Tübingen, Baden-Württemberg"},timezone:"Europe/Berlin"},rA=["condition"],oA="PLAN D6. NO `occupancy`: the indoor-data probe of 2026-07-30 found 3 `indoor=room` elements at Morgenstelle and 0 in the Altstadt, against 2804 at Garching. Room-level analytics are therefore impossible here and the app must not pretend otherwise — buildings stay solid and say why. `condition` lives here instead, because a Sanierungsstau conversation belongs to historic stock, which is exactly what this AOI is. ⚠️ `flow` WAS listed here and has been REMOVED (2026-07-30, Phase 8): decision D5 says Campus Flow is derived from the real lecture timetable, and Tübingen has no room bookings at all to derive it from. The footpath network exists and the Neckarbrücke really is the chokepoint between Altstadt and Wilhelmstraße — but a flow map here could only be invented, and an invented crowd on a named real bridge is exactly the kind of claim this project refuses to make quietly. It can return if a timetable source ever does.",lA={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:9.04,east:9.075,south:48.51,north:48.532,$comment:"HIGH-RESOLUTION CORE, ~2.58 x 2.45 km. Chosen to hold every resolved focus place with margin: Schloss Hohentübingen at the western end (9.0508), Hegelbau at the eastern (9.0623), Hbf to the south (48.5157) and the Kupferbau/Neue Aula ridge to the north (48.5259). That span IS the university — Tübingen has no campus in the Garching sense, the institutes are threaded through a medieval town, and that is the thing worth rendering."},cA={crs:"EPSG:4326",west:8.93,east:9.19,south:48.44,north:48.61,$comment:"COARSE TERRAIN SHELL, ~19.1 x 18.9 km. Unlike Garching, this shell is doing real work: the Neckar valley runs out of the core in both directions and the Schönbuch ridge and the Alb foreland are what a viewer standing on the Schlossberg actually sees on the horizon. Reaches Bebenhausen and the Schönbuch to the north, the Steinlach valley and the Alb foothills to the south, Rottenburg to the west."},uA="EPSG:25832",dA="DHHN2016",hA={min:310,max:445,$comment:"MEASURED 2026-07-30 from the LGL DGM1 mosaic: 312.15 to 439.54 m over the core, 100% coverage. Bracketed slightly wider so the hypsometric ramp does not clip at the extremes. The first estimate here was 295-500, which was a guess from published summit heights and would have wasted a third of the colour ramp on elevations this AOI does not contain. Real landmarks check out: the Neckar at the Eberhardsbrücke reads 317.4 m, the Stiftskirche 340.2 m, Schloss Hohentübingen 370.0 m and the Österberg tops out at 439.5 m. 127 m of relief inside 2.6 km — the OPPOSITE problem to Garching (12 m across the whole core), and why this AOI exists."},fA={maxPx:4096,$comment:"DOP20 via the LGL GeoWebCache layer `DOP_20_C` (GoogleMapsCompatible, EPSG:3857) rather than the 1.5 GB of per-cell ZIPs the portal offers for the same six cells — the mesh underneath is at 4 m posting and a 20 cm drape is neither loadable nor useful. At zoom 18 the service gives 0.597 m per pixel, which lands within a percent of Garching's 0.62 and keeps the two AOIs visually comparable. Reprojected from Web Mercator onto the UTM32 grid, because everything else in this app is UTM32 and a drape that disagrees with the terrain by even a few metres reads as the buildings being misplaced."},mA={sourceResolutionM:1,renderResolutionM:2,renderDecimation:2,$comment:"1 m DGM1 source (LGL), resampled to 2 m, mesh decimated 2x -> 4 m posting. Same grid as Garching so the two AOIs are visually comparable and the renderer has one code path. ~1290 x 1225 samples (~3.2 MB), ~395k mesh vertices. On terrain this steep the 4 m posting is the honest limit of what the 1 m source supports after decimation; going coarser visibly rounds off the Schlossberg."},pA={sourceResolutionM:30,renderResolutionM:30,renderDecimation:3,transitionBandM:1100,$comment:"Copernicus DEM GLO-30 -> ~90 m posting. Wider band than Garching (900 m) because there is real relief to reconcile at the seam: the shell is a SURFACE model that includes the Schönbuch canopy, the core is bare earth, and a forested ridge crossing the boundary is exactly where an unmeasured datum offset becomes a visible step. The offset is measured in the overlap ring, never assumed."},gA=[{id:"schloss",name:"Schloss Hohentübingen",lat:48.51949,lon:9.050794},{id:"neue_aula",name:"Neue Aula",lat:48.5240638,lon:9.0596848},{id:"stiftskirche",name:"Stiftskirche St. Georg",lat:48.520109,lon:9.0560684},{id:"hoelderlinturm",name:"Hölderlinturm",lat:48.5193288,lon:9.055677},{id:"kupferbau",name:"Kupferbau",lat:48.5259241,lon:9.0583541},{id:"alte_burse",name:"Alte Burse",lat:48.5194551,lon:9.0549007},{id:"hegelbau",name:"Hegelbau",lat:48.5259181,lon:9.062273},{id:"rathaus",name:"Rathaus",lat:48.5203431,lon:9.053101},{id:"eberhardsbruecke",name:"Eberhardsbrücke",lat:48.5190123,lon:9.0579405},{id:"platanenallee",name:"Platanenallee",lat:48.5189963,lon:9.0576943},{id:"bahnhof",name:"Tübingen Hbf",lat:48.5157271,lon:9.0557274,kind:"station"}],vA="Resolved 2026-07-30 from OpenStreetMap via Overpass — NOT recalled — and then RE-resolved after the first pass returned three wrong features, which is worth recording because it is the exact failure the verify step exists to catch. A loose name match on 'Hohentübingen' returned the *Sängerschaft* Hohentübingen (a student fraternity, node/5725200864) instead of the castle; 'Hölderlinturm' matched the Lyrikhandlung bookshop next door; 'Rathaus' matched an annex in the Haaggasse. The second pass used tag filters rather than names — historic=castle (relation/19602), amenity=townhall (way/682712527) — and those are the coordinates above. LESSON, same as the Alpine AOI: a name match is not a resolution.",bA={$comment:"⚠️ FULLY SYNTHETIC — PLAN Phase 7 and §6. No German university publishes its Sanierungsstau per building, and inventing one for a named real university is the single most reputationally dangerous thing this app could do quietly. So it is not quiet: every figure derived from this block carries a synthetic badge in the UI, and the generator is seeded and committed so any number on screen can be traced back to a rule rather than to a guess.",seed:20260730,gradeScale:[1,2,3,4,5],gradeDistribution:[.08,.22,.34,.26,.1],$gradeDistributionComment:"Deliberately skewed to grades 3-4. That shape is the widely discussed picture of German university building stock, not a measurement of Tübingen's. It is chosen so the story is recognisable to a Kanzler rather than flattering.",costPerM2ByGrade:{1:0,2:150,3:620,4:1450,5:2600},priorityWeights:{condition:.45,usageIntensity:.25,energy:.2,heritage:.1},scenarios:["nichtstun","priorisiert","gleichverteilt"],horizonYears:{from:2026,to:2040}},yA={authority:"Landesamt für Geoinformation und Landentwicklung Baden-Württemberg (LGL)",licence:"Datenlizenz Deutschland – Namensnennung – Version 2.0",licenceUrl:"https://www.govdata.de/dl-de/by-2-0",attribution:"Datenquelle: LGL, www.lgl-bw.de, dl-de/by-2-0",portal:"https://opengeodata.lgl-bw.de/",products:{dgm:"DGM1",orthophoto:"DOP20",buildings:"LoD2",canopy:"nDOM"},$productsComment:"Verified 2026-07-30 against the LGL Open GeoData offering: DOP20, DGM, DOM1/bDOM/nDOM and LoD1+LoD2 are all published as open data under dl-de/by-2-0, which permits commercial use explicitly. The portal serves PRE-TILED ZIP archives rather than the per-tile GeoTIFF URLs the Bavarian fetcher builds arithmetically, so Phase 6 needs a genuinely new adapter (tools/geodata/fetch_lgl_bw.py) rather than a parameterisation of fetch_bvv.py.",$vegetationComment:"⚠️ Baden-Württemberg publishes NO tree cadastre, so the Bavarian `trees` step has no counterpart here. Vegetation is instead DERIVED from the nDOM (normalised digital surface model = canopy height above bare earth): threshold the canopy, find local maxima as stems, estimate crown radius from height. Fewer trees will be 'measured' than in Bavaria and they should be described as derived, not surveyed — but on the Platanenallee and the Schlossberg they carry most of the scene."},xA={authority:"ESA / DLR / Airbus Defence and Space — Copernicus DEM GLO-30",licence:"Copernicus DEM free licence (worldwide, free reuse with the prescribed notice)",licenceUrl:"https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM",attribution:"produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved",cogUrlTemplate:"https://copernicus-dem-30m.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_{NS}{lat:02d}_00_{EW}{lon:03d}_00_DEM.tif",tiles:["N48_E008","N48_E009"],$tilesComment:"TWO tiles, unlike Garching's one: the shell spans 8.93-9.19 E and therefore crosses the E009 meridian. The fetcher must mosaic them before resampling — a case the Bavarian AOIs never exercised, so treat the first Tübingen shell build as the test of that path."},_A={osm:{authority:"OpenStreetMap contri